1
00:02:30,488 --> 00:02:32,490
I'm calm, steady.

2
00:02:32,657 --> 00:02:35,826
I slept well. 8.2 hours.
No bad dreams.

3
00:02:42,083 --> 00:02:43,751
I am ready to go.

4
00:02:43,918 --> 00:02:46,671
Ready to do my job
to the best of my abilities.

5
00:02:47,713 --> 00:02:50,049
<i>I am focused
only on the essential,</i>

6
00:02:50,132 --> 00:02:51,801
<i>to the exclusion of all else.</i>

7
00:02:53,928 --> 00:02:56,305
I will make
only pragmatic decisions.

8
00:02:57,765 --> 00:03:00,685
<i>I will not allow myself
to be distracted.</i>

9
00:03:00,851 --> 00:03:02,978
<i>I will not allow
my mind to linger</i>

10
00:03:03,062 --> 00:03:04,730
<i>on that which is unimportant.</i>

11
00:03:15,991 --> 00:03:19,954
I will not rely
on anyone or anything.

12
00:03:20,121 --> 00:03:22,707
I will not be
vulnerable to mistakes.

13
00:03:24,959 --> 00:03:28,421
Resting BPM, 47. Submit.

14
00:03:30,715 --> 00:03:32,591
<i>Your psychological evaluation</i>

15
00:03:32,675 --> 00:03:33,759
<i>has been approved.</i>

16
00:03:33,843 --> 00:03:34,844
<i>As a reminder,</i>

17
00:03:34,927 --> 00:03:36,554
<i>please perform any safety
and equipment checks...</i>

18
00:03:36,637 --> 00:03:39,265
<i>I always wanted
to become an astronaut...</i>

19
00:03:40,599 --> 00:03:43,018
<i>for the future
of mankind and all.</i>

20
00:03:46,564 --> 00:03:49,275
<i>At least, that's what
I always told myself.</i>

21
00:03:55,406 --> 00:03:57,992
<i>I see myself from the outside.</i>

22
00:03:58,951 --> 00:04:01,579
<i>Smile, present a side.</i>

23
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:04,749
<i>It's a performance...</i>

24
00:04:05,583 --> 00:04:07,710
<i>with my eye on the exit.</i>

25
00:04:10,045 --> 00:04:11,964
<i>Always on the exit.</i>

26
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:17,261
<i>Just don't touch me.</i>

27
00:04:28,355 --> 00:04:30,566
<i>Take care, Major. Be careful.</i>

28
00:04:30,733 --> 00:04:32,151
<i>Thanks for that.</i>

29
00:04:43,579 --> 00:04:44,997
<i>Roy, Bravo post</i>

30
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:47,374
<i>has got a robotic arm
on 93 Echo...</i>

31
00:04:47,541 --> 00:04:48,834
<i>appears to be malfunctioning.</i>

32
00:04:48,918 --> 00:04:49,919
<i>We're gonna need you to take</i>

33
00:04:50,002 --> 00:04:51,504
<i>a team down there
and check it out.</i>

34
00:04:51,670 --> 00:04:53,130
<i>Run some diagnostics. Over.</i>

35
00:04:53,297 --> 00:04:55,299
<i>Copy that.
Heading that way.</i>

36
00:05:05,184 --> 00:05:06,852
<i>Good morning
to our astronauts up there</i>

37
00:05:06,936 --> 00:05:09,021
<i>on the International
Space Antenna.</i>

38
00:05:09,396 --> 00:05:11,398
<i>Sure is a beautiful day.</i>

39
00:05:11,982 --> 00:05:14,193
<i>Just perfect
to try and contact...</i>

40
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:16,695
<i>our distant neighbors
out there in the heavens.</i>

41
00:05:19,865 --> 00:05:21,283
<i>At least
it's comfortable out here.</i>

42
00:05:21,367 --> 00:05:22,993
<i>I got some scores here.</i>

43
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:27,081
<i>Let's see, it was Iowa State
over Kansas, 35 - 16.</i>

44
00:05:27,623 --> 00:05:29,542
<i>Space I understand.</i>

45
00:05:35,756 --> 00:05:38,175
<i>Control, I have visual
on the arm. Over.</i>

46
00:05:38,342 --> 00:05:39,844
<i>Affirmative, Major.
Proceed.</i>

47
00:05:40,010 --> 00:05:43,180
<i>Copy that.
Moving to the unit now.</i>

48
00:05:54,525 --> 00:05:56,569
<i>Control, I'm seeing
a power surge on C-post.</i>

49
00:05:56,652 --> 00:05:57,736
<i>You getting that?</i>

50
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:58,821
<i>Uh...
Roger that, Roy...</i>

51
00:05:58,904 --> 00:06:00,406
<i>Control, we got a lot
of people up there. Over.</i>

52
00:06:00,489 --> 00:06:02,741
<i>Control. Control,
I think we have some spikes...</i>

53
00:06:02,825 --> 00:06:04,243
<i>Please just stand by,
we're working the issue.</i>

54
00:06:04,326 --> 00:06:05,327
<i>Just stand by.</i>

55
00:06:05,411 --> 00:06:07,329
<i>Control, they're happening everywhere.</i>

56
00:06:24,138 --> 00:06:25,764
<i>Command, cutting power.</i>

57
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:28,392
<i>Get off the tower now!</i>

58
00:06:32,771 --> 00:06:34,273
<i>You've gotta bail out!</i>

59
00:06:44,366 --> 00:06:45,868
<i>Oh, my God!</i>

60
00:07:01,967 --> 00:07:03,719
<i>Control, McBride.</i>

61
00:07:04,970 --> 00:07:06,347
<i>I'm in a spin.</i>

62
00:07:06,430 --> 00:07:08,599
<i>Atmosphere's too thin
to stabilize.</i>

63
00:07:10,434 --> 00:07:13,437
<i>I'm trying to keep
the tumble down,</i>

64
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:15,272
<i>so I don't black out.</i>

65
00:07:18,943 --> 00:07:20,235
<i>Control, do you read?</i>

66
00:08:58,250 --> 00:08:59,960
<i>"A self-destructive side."</i>

67
00:09:01,086 --> 00:09:03,172
<i>That's what
she used to say to me.</i>

68
00:09:05,299 --> 00:09:07,259
<i>I should feel something.</i>

69
00:09:09,219 --> 00:09:10,763
<i>I survived.</i>

70
00:09:12,056 --> 00:09:13,223
<i>I should feel something.</i>

71
00:09:13,307 --> 00:09:15,059
<i>In what has become
known as "The Surge"...</i>

72
00:09:15,142 --> 00:09:17,478
<i>a series of destructive
electrical storms</i>

73
00:09:17,561 --> 00:09:19,396
<i>has wreaked havoc
across the globe...</i>

74
00:09:19,563 --> 00:09:20,856
<i>and scientists are concerned</i>

75
00:09:20,939 --> 00:09:22,900
<i>we've not seen
the last of them yet.</i>

76
00:09:23,067 --> 00:09:25,110
<i>Their origin? Outer space.</i>

77
00:09:25,277 --> 00:09:27,196
<i>The cause? Unknown so far...</i>

78
00:09:28,655 --> 00:09:30,532
<i>This is a message from SPACECOM.</i>

79
00:09:30,699 --> 00:09:32,451
<i>In light of
the recent catastrophe...</i>

80
00:09:32,618 --> 00:09:34,286
<i>your attendance
is required for a debrief...</i>

81
00:09:34,369 --> 00:09:36,789
<i>to be held in Building 91,
Vandersteen Base.</i>

82
00:09:36,872 --> 00:09:39,291
<i>Please note, this meeting will
be classified "top secret."</i>

83
00:09:44,296 --> 00:09:46,173
Roy, how are you? Thanks for coming in.
Appreciate it.

84
00:09:46,256 --> 00:09:47,257
General.

85
00:09:47,341 --> 00:09:49,218
This is Lieutenant
General Rivas, Director of

86
00:09:49,301 --> 00:09:50,844
U.S. SPACECOM Special Ops.
Hi.

87
00:09:50,928 --> 00:09:51,929
Sir.
Major.

88
00:09:52,012 --> 00:09:53,222
Adjutant General Vogel,
head of Security.

89
00:09:53,305 --> 00:09:54,556
Major.
Ma'am.

90
00:09:54,723 --> 00:09:56,266
They flew
all the way in from Virginia

91
00:09:56,350 --> 00:09:57,935
just last night,
just to see you.

92
00:09:58,102 --> 00:09:59,269
Well, thank you.

93
00:09:59,436 --> 00:10:01,939
Your, uh, profile
is certainly very impressive.

94
00:10:02,106 --> 00:10:04,942
You've done exceptionally well
on all the assessment tests.

95
00:10:05,109 --> 00:10:07,111
Basic combat, space training.

96
00:10:07,194 --> 00:10:08,862
Just exceptional
across the board.

97
00:10:09,446 --> 00:10:10,614
The rumor is that

98
00:10:10,697 --> 00:10:13,033
your pulse rate
has never gone above 80...

99
00:10:13,117 --> 00:10:14,660
in any of the spacewalks,
skywalks,

100
00:10:14,743 --> 00:10:15,744
and even on
this most recent fall.

101
00:10:15,828 --> 00:10:16,829
Is that correct?

102
00:10:17,246 --> 00:10:18,539
Well, so far, sir.

103
00:10:18,705 --> 00:10:19,957
That's very impressive.

104
00:10:20,499 --> 00:10:22,835
According to this,
married once, no children?

105
00:10:23,001 --> 00:10:24,336
Yes, sir.

106
00:10:25,003 --> 00:10:27,214
It's dangerous business,
as we know.

107
00:10:27,297 --> 00:10:29,174
Best not to
subject others to it.

108
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:31,135
Fair enough.

109
00:10:31,718 --> 00:10:32,845
Well, we didn't
bring you in here

110
00:10:32,928 --> 00:10:34,930
to talk about your fall, Roy.

111
00:10:36,348 --> 00:10:37,474
We have something...

112
00:10:37,641 --> 00:10:42,104
of a highly classified nature
to show you.

113
00:10:45,107 --> 00:10:46,400
Please have a seat, Major.

114
00:10:46,859 --> 00:10:47,943
Yes, ma'am.

115
00:10:54,825 --> 00:10:56,493
What you are about to see are

116
00:10:56,577 --> 00:10:58,620
spectrogram images of Neptune.

117
00:10:59,955 --> 00:11:02,666
These are cosmic ray bursts.

118
00:11:02,833 --> 00:11:05,460
That was taken just 11 days ago.

119
00:11:06,044 --> 00:11:08,130
It released
high-energy particles...

120
00:11:08,213 --> 00:11:10,799
that caused
a catastrophic power surge

121
00:11:10,883 --> 00:11:12,801
all over the world.

122
00:11:13,677 --> 00:11:16,221
And that's what
almost killed you.

123
00:11:17,848 --> 00:11:19,141
The rays grow stronger

124
00:11:19,224 --> 00:11:21,476
as they radiate towards us
here on Earth.

125
00:11:27,107 --> 00:11:30,569
Major, what can you tell us
about the Lima Project?

126
00:11:35,073 --> 00:11:38,118
First manned expedition to
the outer solar system, sir.

127
00:11:39,536 --> 00:11:42,873
Some 29 years ago, as you know.

128
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:45,792
And the commander was...

129
00:11:45,959 --> 00:11:48,045
He was my father, sir.

130
00:11:49,004 --> 00:11:50,005
The ship disappeared

131
00:11:50,088 --> 00:11:52,549
approximately 16 years
into the mission.

132
00:11:52,716 --> 00:11:54,426
No data was ever recovered.

133
00:11:54,509 --> 00:11:56,678
Deep space missions
were halted after that.

134
00:11:58,013 --> 00:11:59,681
Yes, that's him.

135
00:11:59,848 --> 00:12:03,060
Can you tell us how you
handled your father's absence?

136
00:12:04,895 --> 00:12:06,396
Well...

137
00:12:09,483 --> 00:12:11,693
My mother was
certainly distressed by it.

138
00:12:11,777 --> 00:12:13,820
Uh, she was quite ill
at the time.

139
00:12:14,321 --> 00:12:17,366
But he was,
uh, committed to his job...

140
00:12:17,532 --> 00:12:19,660
and I'm sure it was very
difficult for him as well.

141
00:12:20,994 --> 00:12:22,120
Roy...

142
00:12:22,829 --> 00:12:26,833
we have something that might
come as quite a shock to you.

143
00:12:29,628 --> 00:12:33,715
We believe your father
is still alive near Neptune.

144
00:12:33,882 --> 00:12:35,425
Where exactly, we do not know.

145
00:12:35,592 --> 00:12:37,135
Now, we've sent out
numerous drones,

146
00:12:37,219 --> 00:12:39,554
but obviously,
it's a vast area to cover.

147
00:12:45,811 --> 00:12:48,605
My father's alive, sir?

148
00:12:48,981 --> 00:12:50,524
We believe so.

149
00:12:51,316 --> 00:12:53,610
Roy, The Surge
seems to be the result

150
00:12:53,694 --> 00:12:56,029
of some kind
of anti-matter reaction.

151
00:12:56,697 --> 00:12:59,283
Now, the Lima Project was
powered by that material...

152
00:12:59,449 --> 00:13:01,326
and your father
was in charge of it.

153
00:13:02,035 --> 00:13:03,036
Now, we're talking about

154
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:06,081
a potentially unstoppable
chain reaction here.

155
00:13:06,999 --> 00:13:09,167
The uncontrolled release
of anti-matter...

156
00:13:09,251 --> 00:13:10,627
could ultimately threaten

157
00:13:10,711 --> 00:13:13,463
the stability of
our entire solar system.

158
00:13:14,131 --> 00:13:16,717
All life could be destroyed.

159
00:13:18,176 --> 00:13:21,013
Major, we would like you to send

160
00:13:21,096 --> 00:13:23,974
a personal message on Mars
by secure laser...

161
00:13:24,057 --> 00:13:27,394
to what we hope
is the Lima Project.

162
00:13:27,728 --> 00:13:28,770
The text of your message

163
00:13:28,854 --> 00:13:31,064
would be prepared in advance,
of course.

164
00:13:31,231 --> 00:13:33,734
Mars, sir?
I'm going to Mars?

165
00:13:34,359 --> 00:13:37,779
It is the last secure hub
we have.

166
00:13:39,239 --> 00:13:41,700
Roy, we need to find out

167
00:13:41,783 --> 00:13:43,910
just what we're up against here.

168
00:13:44,077 --> 00:13:45,537
Our underground Mars base

169
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:49,291
was the only one
unaffected by The Surge.

170
00:13:49,458 --> 00:13:51,168
And we believe a personal plea,

171
00:13:51,251 --> 00:13:54,421
from you to your father,
might elicit a response.

172
00:13:54,588 --> 00:13:56,340
We can track that signal...

173
00:13:56,506 --> 00:14:00,093
locate him and figure out
a way to stop this.

174
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:05,766
What is happening out there is
a crisis of unknown magnitude.

175
00:14:05,932 --> 00:14:09,019
Now, we're counting on you
to help us find him.

176
00:14:09,186 --> 00:14:11,021
Are you with us?

177
00:14:14,441 --> 00:14:16,276
Yes, I am, sir.
Good.

178
00:14:16,943 --> 00:14:18,445
You deploy first to the moon.

179
00:14:18,612 --> 00:14:19,905
Our long-range rockets

180
00:14:19,988 --> 00:14:21,323
are stationed there
on the Far Side.

181
00:14:21,406 --> 00:14:23,116
Everything after that will be
on a need-to-know basis.

182
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:24,201
Yes, sir.

183
00:14:24,368 --> 00:14:26,370
Given the magnitude
of the threat...

184
00:14:26,536 --> 00:14:30,290
a cover story is being
formulated to avoid all panic.

185
00:14:30,457 --> 00:14:32,584
You'll be traveling
commercially to the moon

186
00:14:32,667 --> 00:14:33,877
to keep a low profile.

187
00:14:34,044 --> 00:14:36,463
Colonel Pruitt will be your
point person from here on.

188
00:14:36,630 --> 00:14:39,716
Absolute top secrecy
must be maintained.

189
00:14:40,592 --> 00:14:42,260
<i>"Are you with us?"</i>

190
00:14:44,346 --> 00:14:45,972
<i>Like I have a choice.</i>

191
00:14:48,558 --> 00:14:50,811
<i>My dad was a pioneer.</i>

192
00:14:50,977 --> 00:14:54,022
<i>He sacrificed himself for the
search for intelligent life.</i>

193
00:14:55,524 --> 00:14:57,401
<i>My dad was the program.</i>

194
00:14:59,319 --> 00:15:02,239
<i>I was 16 when he left,
29 when he disappeared.</i>

195
00:15:02,406 --> 00:15:05,492
<i>Archived message,
received 27 years...</i>

196
00:15:05,659 --> 00:15:08,036
<i>3 months, 2 days ago.
And that's that.</i>

197
00:15:08,578 --> 00:15:12,124
<i>Roy, this is
a message from your father.</i>

198
00:15:12,290 --> 00:15:15,168
<i>I'm coming at you
from the Lima Project.</i>

199
00:15:15,335 --> 00:15:18,797
<i>Just on our way past Jupiter
and ultimately on to Neptune.</i>

200
00:15:19,297 --> 00:15:21,341
<i>I know you have seen</i>

201
00:15:21,425 --> 00:15:24,219
<i>that we have excited
real and enormous interest...</i>

202
00:15:24,302 --> 00:15:27,848
<i>around the world,
and we are grateful for it.</i>

203
00:15:28,306 --> 00:15:30,475
<i>We're doing big things
up here, real big.</i>

204
00:15:31,685 --> 00:15:34,938
<i>Namely, we're about to answer
the number one question...</i>

205
00:15:35,105 --> 00:15:38,525
<i>when do we find all the
intelligent life out there?</i>

206
00:15:38,692 --> 00:15:40,110
<i>And we know we will.</i>

207
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:42,571
<i>We're going to the edge
of the heliosphere...</i>

208
00:15:42,737 --> 00:15:44,281
<i>where the sun's magnetic field</i>

209
00:15:44,364 --> 00:15:46,992
<i>won't affect
our instruments one bit.</i>

210
00:15:47,159 --> 00:15:51,246
<i>We'll be able to examine any
star system for complex life.</i>

211
00:15:51,413 --> 00:15:54,082
<i>Never been done before,
and we sure are optimistic.</i>

212
00:15:54,666 --> 00:15:58,211
<i>I feel your energy back home,
and of course, I think of God.</i>

213
00:15:58,378 --> 00:16:03,133
<i>I'm overwhelmed at seeing
and feeling His presence...</i>

214
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,635
<i>so close.</i>

215
00:16:05,802 --> 00:16:07,304
<i>I love you, my son.</i>

216
00:16:13,435 --> 00:16:14,644
Hello, Roy.

217
00:16:17,689 --> 00:16:19,816
I'm here to go
on this trip with you.

218
00:16:20,692 --> 00:16:22,152
Keep my eye on ya.

219
00:16:22,611 --> 00:16:25,238
Colonel Pruitt,
good to meet you.

220
00:16:26,406 --> 00:16:27,449
Actually...

221
00:16:29,326 --> 00:16:30,535
we've met.

222
00:16:31,203 --> 00:16:34,331
It was a long time ago.
I knew your dad.

223
00:16:35,415 --> 00:16:37,250
We were close, he and I.

224
00:16:37,417 --> 00:16:41,129
We started out together,
went to Purdue together.

225
00:16:42,172 --> 00:16:43,882
He was a brilliant man.

226
00:16:44,049 --> 00:16:46,009
I know.
Yeah.

227
00:16:46,176 --> 00:16:48,470
And I remember going
to the house and seeing you.

228
00:16:48,637 --> 00:16:50,680
You were running around
everywhere.

229
00:16:50,847 --> 00:16:53,183
You drove your
poor mother nuts, but...

230
00:16:53,725 --> 00:16:55,143
How do you feel?

231
00:16:59,189 --> 00:17:00,982
Is this part of my psych eval?

232
00:17:01,274 --> 00:17:03,443
Uh...

233
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:05,612
No, not really, but yes.

234
00:17:05,779 --> 00:17:08,740
I mean, you're going
to be monitored constantly...

235
00:17:08,907 --> 00:17:12,661
your mental state,
your emotional state.

236
00:17:12,827 --> 00:17:15,705
You have a direct connection
with the subject.

237
00:17:16,873 --> 00:17:20,293
Colonel, for what it's worth,
I think my father's dead.

238
00:17:25,215 --> 00:17:27,050
Yeah, um...

239
00:17:27,217 --> 00:17:32,597
I was a lunar astronaut
for SPACECOM for 31 years.

240
00:17:33,265 --> 00:17:36,726
And I came to the
realization out there...

241
00:17:36,893 --> 00:17:40,355
a voyage of exploration
can be used

242
00:17:40,438 --> 00:17:43,275
for something
as simple as escape.

243
00:17:43,858 --> 00:17:45,986
I'm telling you this, Roy,

244
00:17:46,069 --> 00:17:50,115
because we have to
hold out the possibility...

245
00:17:50,282 --> 00:17:53,868
that your father
may be hiding from us.

246
00:17:58,540 --> 00:18:00,458
Do you think you're ready to go?

247
00:18:03,169 --> 00:18:04,588
I'm ready.

248
00:18:04,754 --> 00:18:05,839
All right.

249
00:18:25,150 --> 00:18:26,943
<i>Your pre-launch quarantine</i>

250
00:18:27,027 --> 00:18:28,903
<i>is almost complete.</i>

251
00:18:29,237 --> 00:18:30,447
<i>You have shown no evidence</i>

252
00:18:30,530 --> 00:18:31,656
<i>of bacterial
or viral infection...</i>

253
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:34,659
<i>So many times in my life,
I've screwed up.</i>

254
00:18:34,743 --> 00:18:36,286
<i>Although all efforts have been made...</i>

255
00:18:36,369 --> 00:18:39,497
<i>I've talked,
when I should have listened.</i>

256
00:18:39,664 --> 00:18:41,249
<i>I've been harsh,</i>

257
00:18:41,333 --> 00:18:43,209
<i>when I should have been tender.</i>

258
00:18:44,002 --> 00:18:46,087
<i>In the event
of illness or accident...</i>

259
00:18:46,171 --> 00:18:47,172
<i>please make certain</i>

260
00:18:47,255 --> 00:18:49,341
<i>that you have listed
any family members...</i>

261
00:18:49,507 --> 00:18:51,051
<i>spouse, or significant other</i>

262
00:18:51,134 --> 00:18:53,136
<i>as your next of kin,
in your personal file.</i>

263
00:18:53,303 --> 00:18:54,638
Volume down.

264
00:18:56,389 --> 00:18:59,559
Message.
Personal directory. Eve.

265
00:19:02,979 --> 00:19:04,773
Hi, Eve, it's Roy.

266
00:19:06,524 --> 00:19:07,525
Uh...

267
00:19:07,609 --> 00:19:10,236
I'm away again,
no surprise there.

268
00:19:13,073 --> 00:19:14,741
I just wanted to say...

269
00:19:24,751 --> 00:19:27,587
<i>I made a promise
to always be truthful.</i>

270
00:19:28,588 --> 00:19:29,756
<i>But I wasn't.</i>

271
00:19:29,923 --> 00:19:33,134
Listen, I wanted to say...

272
00:19:39,015 --> 00:19:40,934
I didn't want you to go.

273
00:19:44,437 --> 00:19:45,522
Delete.

274
00:19:47,482 --> 00:19:48,566
Cancel.

275
00:19:51,653 --> 00:19:52,821
<i>Good morning.</i>

276
00:19:52,904 --> 00:19:54,864
<i>I've been trained
to compartmentalize.</i>

277
00:19:55,031 --> 00:19:56,866
<i>SPACECOM requires you
to complete</i>

278
00:19:56,950 --> 00:19:58,952
<i>a pre-launch
psychological evaluation.</i>

279
00:19:59,119 --> 00:20:01,579
<i>It seems to me
that's how I approach my life.</i>

280
00:20:02,622 --> 00:20:06,292
Resting BPM is 56.

281
00:20:08,586 --> 00:20:11,381
Didn't sleep much last night,
but it shouldn't be a problem.

282
00:20:11,548 --> 00:20:13,550
I remain mission ready.

283
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:16,761
<i>You have been approved</i>

284
00:20:16,845 --> 00:20:18,054
<i>for lunar travel.</i>

285
00:20:23,268 --> 00:20:25,395
<i>Is it your first time
to the moon?</i>

286
00:20:25,854 --> 00:20:27,856
No, but it's been a while.

287
00:20:28,022 --> 00:20:29,607
Are you planning
on traveling outside

288
00:20:29,691 --> 00:20:30,942
the secure zone on your visit?

289
00:20:31,109 --> 00:20:32,193
No.

290
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:33,361
Again.

291
00:20:34,028 --> 00:20:35,572
How's that?
Okay.

292
00:20:35,655 --> 00:20:37,365
Okay, not too snug?
Yeah, it feels all right.

293
00:20:38,825 --> 00:20:40,076
Breathe.

294
00:20:40,702 --> 00:20:42,704
<i>Virgin flight 6092,</i>

295
00:20:42,787 --> 00:20:45,081
<i>to Tycho Base, Moon,
boarding now.</i>

296
00:20:51,004 --> 00:20:52,172
Welcome aboard, sir.

297
00:20:52,255 --> 00:20:53,256
I'm Captain Lu.
Thank you.

298
00:20:53,423 --> 00:20:54,674
Hi, Captain.
Watch the step.

299
00:20:54,758 --> 00:20:56,217
Duck your head.
Okay.

300
00:20:58,386 --> 00:21:00,138
Hello, welcome. Flight pack?
Hello.

301
00:21:00,305 --> 00:21:01,306
Yes, thanks.
Great.

302
00:21:01,389 --> 00:21:03,308
Third seat, to your right.
Okay.

303
00:21:05,518 --> 00:21:06,519
Excuse me.

304
00:21:07,312 --> 00:21:08,730
Hello.
Hello.

305
00:21:37,801 --> 00:21:39,093
<i>We remind you,</i>

306
00:21:39,177 --> 00:21:40,845
<i>the moon is borderless.</i>

307
00:21:41,012 --> 00:21:43,139
<i>Many mining zones
are disputed territory</i>

308
00:21:43,223 --> 00:21:44,974
<i>and considered to be
in a state of war.</i>

309
00:21:45,517 --> 00:21:47,519
<i>Please stay within
the restricted, safe area...</i>

310
00:21:47,685 --> 00:21:48,937
Excuse me?

311
00:21:49,103 --> 00:21:50,939
May I have a blanket
and pillow pack please?

312
00:21:51,105 --> 00:21:53,316
Sure. $125.

313
00:21:53,817 --> 00:21:55,068
<i>Payment accepted.</i>

314
00:21:55,151 --> 00:21:56,653
Thank you.
Thank you.

315
00:22:16,047 --> 00:22:17,257
<i>As we approach,</i>

316
00:22:17,340 --> 00:22:19,259
<i>some of you can see
the grand telescope array...</i>

317
00:22:19,425 --> 00:22:20,635
<i>near the Atlas crater.</i>

318
00:22:20,802 --> 00:22:22,637
<i>It's the moon's largest facility</i>

319
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,597
<i>for extraterrestrial research.</i>

320
00:22:26,641 --> 00:22:27,725
Hot towel?

321
00:22:27,809 --> 00:22:29,310
Oh, thank you.
Thank you for flying with us.

322
00:22:29,394 --> 00:22:30,895
We do appreciate it.

323
00:22:31,563 --> 00:22:33,565
<i>Please prepare for landing.</i>

324
00:23:05,722 --> 00:23:08,433
<i>All the hopes we ever
had for space travel...</i>

325
00:23:08,725 --> 00:23:12,437
<i>covered up by drink stands
and T-shirt vendors.</i>

326
00:23:12,770 --> 00:23:15,773
<i>Just a recreation of what
we're running from on Earth.</i>

327
00:23:18,484 --> 00:23:20,486
<i>We are world-eaters.</i>

328
00:23:21,654 --> 00:23:24,240
<i>If my dad could see this now...</i>

329
00:23:24,407 --> 00:23:27,035
<i>he'd tear it all down.</i>

330
00:23:36,002 --> 00:23:38,421
Our rocket is named <i>Cepheus.</i>

331
00:23:39,255 --> 00:23:41,716
The crew will be
SPACECOM military personnel.

332
00:23:42,634 --> 00:23:45,303
They're completely unaware
of our mission.

333
00:23:45,470 --> 00:23:47,138
We have to keep it that way.

334
00:23:47,305 --> 00:23:50,558
The launchpad is on the
other side of no man's land.

335
00:23:50,725 --> 00:23:53,019
It's very dangerous...

336
00:23:53,186 --> 00:23:55,021
so we'll have armed personnel

337
00:23:55,104 --> 00:23:58,066
to protect us and escort us
to the Far Side.

338
00:24:01,861 --> 00:24:04,697
Colonel, can I ask
what the last conversation

339
00:24:04,781 --> 00:24:06,366
you had with my dad was?

340
00:24:07,909 --> 00:24:09,619
It was not very pleasant.

341
00:24:10,662 --> 00:24:13,873
We quarreled about
my leaving the program.

342
00:24:15,792 --> 00:24:18,378
He accused me
of being a traitor.

343
00:24:20,797 --> 00:24:22,966
And if you were to find him...

344
00:24:23,132 --> 00:24:25,009
then what?

345
00:24:26,260 --> 00:24:29,013
Is this very difficult
for you, son?

346
00:24:29,180 --> 00:24:30,765
This being about your father?

347
00:24:33,476 --> 00:24:34,477
No.

348
00:24:35,228 --> 00:24:37,689
No, my dad's a hero.

349
00:24:37,855 --> 00:24:40,358
SPACECOM's trying
to impugn a man

350
00:24:40,441 --> 00:24:42,443
who's given his entire life
to the program.

351
00:24:42,610 --> 00:24:44,362
I think it's despicable.

352
00:24:45,571 --> 00:24:47,240
Or desperate at best.

353
00:24:51,536 --> 00:24:53,621
<i>We are approaching Terminal R,</i>

354
00:24:53,705 --> 00:24:54,789
<i>lunar rover hangar.</i>

355
00:24:54,956 --> 00:24:57,959
We've been having trouble
with pirates since September.

356
00:24:58,751 --> 00:25:00,628
Some countries have been
giving them safe haven.

357
00:25:00,795 --> 00:25:03,172
They'll take hostages
or go for our rovers.

358
00:25:03,881 --> 00:25:06,009
It's like the Wild West
out there...

359
00:25:06,175 --> 00:25:08,553
but we'll get you
to your spacecraft.

360
00:25:10,763 --> 00:25:12,390
This your first time
in a war zone?

361
00:25:12,974 --> 00:25:14,767
Three years over
the Arctic Circle.

362
00:25:14,934 --> 00:25:16,144
All right.

363
00:25:16,310 --> 00:25:18,187
And a heck of a lot
of Army-Navy games.

364
00:25:18,563 --> 00:25:20,606
Well, I guess there's not much

365
00:25:20,690 --> 00:25:21,816
you haven't seen, right?

366
00:25:22,191 --> 00:25:23,985
Well, look,
it's almost a full moon.

367
00:25:24,152 --> 00:25:26,112
A large stretch of the
Far Side's real black,

368
00:25:26,195 --> 00:25:27,780
so let's suit up.

369
00:25:28,239 --> 00:25:29,574
<i>Lunar Rovers, Group C,</i>

370
00:25:29,657 --> 00:25:30,742
<i>set for departure...</i>

371
00:25:30,825 --> 00:25:34,537
<i>to the Far Side launch complex
through gate 12.</i>

372
00:25:34,704 --> 00:25:37,081
<i>Please maintain
situational awareness.</i>

373
00:25:56,559 --> 00:25:58,519
<i>Rover 7, confirming settings.</i>

374
00:25:59,020 --> 00:26:01,272
<i>Bearing two-niner-oh.</i>

375
00:26:43,022 --> 00:26:44,190
<i>Roy?</i>

376
00:26:44,357 --> 00:26:45,399
<i>Yes, Colonel.</i>

377
00:26:45,566 --> 00:26:49,612
<i>Look at it.
The big blue marble.</i>

378
00:26:50,196 --> 00:26:52,865
<i>Never ceases to amaze me</i>

379
00:27:15,805 --> 00:27:17,765
<i>Lieutenant, you clocking this?</i>

380
00:27:17,932 --> 00:27:19,308
<i>Yeah, same here.</i>

381
00:27:19,475 --> 00:27:21,727
<i>I can't ID any
national markings. Over.</i>

382
00:27:21,894 --> 00:27:23,229
<i>Lieutenant...
At 7 o'clock...</i>

383
00:27:23,312 --> 00:27:25,606
<i>Alpha, what do we got here?</i>

384
00:27:26,482 --> 00:27:28,109
<i>Alpha, we have what looks like</i>

385
00:27:28,192 --> 00:27:31,070
<i>unidentified rovers
approaching our position.</i>

386
00:27:31,237 --> 00:27:32,238
<i>Possible pirate activity,</i>

387
00:27:32,321 --> 00:27:33,906
<i>and I got a couple
of VIPs with me.</i>

388
00:27:34,073 --> 00:27:35,575
<i>Roger, moving to flank you.</i>

389
00:27:35,741 --> 00:27:39,036
<i>Uh, Alpha, we may need
some ballistics help up here.</i>

390
00:27:39,203 --> 00:27:40,288
<i>Potential hostile situation...</i>

391
00:27:40,454 --> 00:27:44,041
<i>Here we go again,
fighting over resources.</i>

392
00:27:44,208 --> 00:27:45,960
<i>We got two coming up
on our rear, 7 o'clock.</i>

393
00:27:46,043 --> 00:27:47,336
<i>Appears to be pirates,</i>

394
00:27:47,420 --> 00:27:48,588
<i>possibly looking for valuables.</i>

395
00:27:48,754 --> 00:27:50,506
<i>We'll send
ballistic support ASAP.</i>

396
00:27:50,590 --> 00:27:52,800
<i>What the hell am I doing here?</i>

397
00:27:57,597 --> 00:27:58,598
<i>Shit!</i>

398
00:27:58,681 --> 00:27:59,807
<i>Alpha, we need backup ASAP!</i>

399
00:27:59,891 --> 00:28:01,350
<i>We're being ambushed!</i>

400
00:28:01,934 --> 00:28:03,686
<i>Mayday, mayday, mayday!
Give me a weapon!</i>

401
00:28:03,853 --> 00:28:05,104
<i>Just hold on!</i>

402
00:28:09,942 --> 00:28:11,277
<i>LRV-3 down.</i>

403
00:28:12,945 --> 00:28:14,530
<i>LRV-2 down.</i>

404
00:28:16,449 --> 00:28:18,326
<i>Alpha, we're gonna go off path</i>

405
00:28:18,409 --> 00:28:19,535
<i>to reach the Far Side.</i>

406
00:28:23,539 --> 00:28:24,540
<i>I have a puncture!</i>

407
00:28:24,707 --> 00:28:27,293
<i>Roy!
I have a puncture.</i>

408
00:28:33,549 --> 00:28:34,759
<i>Roy, you all right?</i>

409
00:28:34,926 --> 00:28:35,927
<i>I'm okay.</i>

410
00:28:36,010 --> 00:28:37,261
<i>Alpha, repeat, we need...</i>

411
00:28:38,471 --> 00:28:40,473
<i>Lieutenant!
Oh, Lord!</i>

412
00:28:43,517 --> 00:28:45,186
<i>Go, go, go.</i>

413
00:28:46,562 --> 00:28:47,813
<i>Hey, break it up.</i>

414
00:28:48,522 --> 00:28:50,900
<i>We are not clear.
I repeat, we are not clear.</i>

415
00:28:51,067 --> 00:28:53,027
<i>We have multiple
enemy craft in pursuit.</i>

416
00:28:53,945 --> 00:28:55,905
<i>Roy!
They're trying to ram us!</i>

417
00:29:05,915 --> 00:29:07,792
<i>Command, Lieutenant is KIA.</i>

418
00:29:07,875 --> 00:29:09,043
<i>We've lost our escort.</i>

419
00:29:09,210 --> 00:29:10,920
<i>Request immediate support.
Over.</i>

420
00:30:31,917 --> 00:30:33,252
<i>Command,</i>

421
00:30:33,336 --> 00:30:35,463
<i>the Lieutenant's body
can be recovered...</i>

422
00:30:35,629 --> 00:30:37,882
<i>just outside Walther crater.</i>

423
00:30:38,924 --> 00:30:41,260
<i>Sorry for the loss.</i>

424
00:30:41,886 --> 00:30:42,887
<i>Over.</i>

425
00:30:43,971 --> 00:30:45,181
<i>Roger that, Major.</i>

426
00:30:46,599 --> 00:30:48,601
<i>Uh, Colonel Pruitt,
we're picking up</i>

427
00:30:48,684 --> 00:30:50,478
<i>an irregular heartbeat
through your system.</i>

428
00:30:51,270 --> 00:30:53,647
<i>We suggest you get that
checked out immediately.</i>

429
00:30:54,523 --> 00:30:56,859
<i>He's supposed to be
my security blanket.</i>

430
00:30:57,485 --> 00:30:59,278
<i>I'm fine.</i>

431
00:30:59,779 --> 00:31:01,614
<i>Why does he still do it?</i>

432
00:31:02,365 --> 00:31:04,784
<i>Why can't he just let go?</i>

433
00:31:10,915 --> 00:31:13,125
<i>My dad couldn't either.</i>

434
00:31:13,584 --> 00:31:15,419
<i>Major, we've been expecting you.</i>

435
00:31:15,586 --> 00:31:17,671
If you have any personal
business you need to tend to,

436
00:31:17,755 --> 00:31:19,090
I suggest doing it now.

437
00:31:20,132 --> 00:31:22,218
Your rocket
will leave momentarily.

438
00:31:22,385 --> 00:31:23,386
Stand down, Sergeant.

439
00:31:23,552 --> 00:31:24,553
Yes, sir.

440
00:31:25,888 --> 00:31:29,600
Roy, just let me sit down.

441
00:31:30,559 --> 00:31:32,895
Colonel, what is it?

442
00:31:35,106 --> 00:31:38,734
I'm not going to be able
to go with you to Mars.

443
00:31:39,318 --> 00:31:42,405
But there are things
you need to know, Roy.

444
00:31:44,698 --> 00:31:46,450
Every minute counts.

445
00:31:46,617 --> 00:31:47,868
Cepheus <i>crew,</i>

446
00:31:47,952 --> 00:31:49,203
<i>prepare for pre-launch checks.</i>

447
00:31:49,787 --> 00:31:54,417
SPACECOM communicated with me.

448
00:31:54,959 --> 00:31:57,002
It is classified.

449
00:31:58,587 --> 00:31:59,880
Take it.

450
00:32:06,470 --> 00:32:08,556
It will put you at great risk.

451
00:32:09,014 --> 00:32:12,184
They do not trust you
on SPACECOM.

452
00:32:13,310 --> 00:32:15,187
But it is crucial...

453
00:32:17,106 --> 00:32:18,149
Sergeant!

454
00:32:18,315 --> 00:32:20,317
<i>Commencing pre-launch checks.</i>

455
00:32:20,484 --> 00:32:23,320
You have to go, Roy. Go.

456
00:32:24,655 --> 00:32:25,698
Go!

457
00:32:39,879 --> 00:32:41,839
<i>Captain, Major McBride,
com check.</i>

458
00:32:42,298 --> 00:32:43,424
<i>Loud and clear, sir.</i>

459
00:32:43,507 --> 00:32:44,508
<i>Welcome aboard the</i> Cepheus.

460
00:32:45,301 --> 00:32:47,470
<i>I'll be hitching a ride
with you if that's all right.</i>

461
00:32:47,636 --> 00:32:49,054
<i>Yes, we were alerted, sir.</i>

462
00:32:49,138 --> 00:32:51,348
<i>On our way to Mars,
the very last stop.</i>

463
00:32:51,515 --> 00:32:53,267
<i>We had two joining us?</i>

464
00:32:53,434 --> 00:32:55,519
<i>It'll just be one, I'm afraid.</i>

465
00:32:55,853 --> 00:32:59,023
<i>Well, we still like you,
Major... McBride!</i>

466
00:32:59,690 --> 00:33:01,275
<i>I think we might
just have ourselves</i>

467
00:33:01,358 --> 00:33:03,486
<i>the son of a legend
onboard with us, team.</i>

468
00:33:03,652 --> 00:33:05,696
<i>Roy, son of Clifford McBride.</i>

469
00:33:05,863 --> 00:33:07,072
<i>Oh, wow!</i>

470
00:33:07,239 --> 00:33:09,617
<i>How 'bout that?
Best in the galaxy.</i>

471
00:33:09,783 --> 00:33:10,868
<i>Welcome aboard, sir.</i>

472
00:33:10,951 --> 00:33:13,204
<i>They are scientists
and technicians...</i>

473
00:33:14,872 --> 00:33:16,707
<i>long haulers.</i>

474
00:33:18,584 --> 00:33:20,753
<i>Captain, could you
contact Control, and ask</i>

475
00:33:20,836 --> 00:33:22,963
<i>about the condition
of a Colonel Pruitt?</i>

476
00:33:23,130 --> 00:33:24,632
<i>Sure, will do now, sir.</i>

477
00:33:24,798 --> 00:33:26,509
<i>SPACECOM, could we get a status...</i>

478
00:33:26,675 --> 00:33:29,094
<i>They seem at ease
with themselves.</i>

479
00:33:29,553 --> 00:33:31,931
<i>What must that be like?</i>

480
00:33:32,473 --> 00:33:36,101
<i>Major, the Colonel was taken
for emergency surgery.</i>

481
00:33:37,186 --> 00:33:38,979
<i>Copy.
Check list complete.</i>

482
00:33:39,146 --> 00:33:40,606
<i>They're oblivious to my purpose.</i>

483
00:33:40,773 --> 00:33:42,691
<i>Destination, Ersa Research Station, Mars.</i>

484
00:33:42,858 --> 00:33:45,986
<i>The last manned outpost
in our solar system.</i>

485
00:33:46,153 --> 00:33:49,782
<i>Duration 19 days,
14 hours and 33 minutes. Over.</i>

486
00:33:51,033 --> 00:33:53,702
<i>Dear Saint Christopher,
protect me today</i>

487
00:33:53,786 --> 00:33:56,288
<i>in all my travels
along the road's way.</i>

488
00:33:56,455 --> 00:33:59,416
<i>Give me your warning sign
if danger is near.</i>

489
00:33:59,583 --> 00:34:01,418
<i>So that I may stop...</i>

490
00:34:16,016 --> 00:34:19,103
<i>Perfect, cue the minibar.</i>

491
00:34:19,270 --> 00:34:22,189
<i>Command, we're gonna give out
the mood stabilizers now.</i>

492
00:34:22,356 --> 00:34:24,316
<i>Our psych evals to follow.</i>

493
00:34:24,692 --> 00:34:25,693
<i>Frank.</i>

494
00:34:25,859 --> 00:34:27,778
<i>'Cause Lord knows
SPACECOM wouldn't want you...</i>

495
00:34:27,945 --> 00:34:29,488
<i>getting all emotional</i>

496
00:34:29,572 --> 00:34:31,073
<i>on us up here, again.</i>

497
00:34:33,659 --> 00:34:34,660
<i>Deavers.</i>

498
00:34:36,537 --> 00:34:37,538
<i>Major?</i>

499
00:34:39,623 --> 00:34:41,250
<i>Get me one of those, candy man.</i>

500
00:34:41,834 --> 00:34:42,835
<i>Captain.</i>

501
00:34:48,257 --> 00:34:50,301
<i>Captain, I have a small
oxygen leak in my suit.</i>

502
00:34:50,384 --> 00:34:51,802
<i>I'm just gonna check my patch.</i>

503
00:34:54,096 --> 00:34:56,181
<i>Have fun back there.</i>

504
00:34:56,265 --> 00:34:58,976
<i>We'll let you know
if we spot any ETs.</i>

505
00:34:59,059 --> 00:35:00,728
<i>Hello, SPACECOM.</i>

506
00:35:00,894 --> 00:35:04,732
<i>We're out here,</i> Cepheus <i>responding.
Smooth sailing.</i>

507
00:35:05,232 --> 00:35:06,483
<i>Roger,</i> Cepheus,

508
00:35:06,567 --> 00:35:07,985
<i>we have your telemetry.</i>

509
00:35:13,532 --> 00:35:15,618
Boys and girls,
time for some Cidofovir.

510
00:35:15,701 --> 00:35:17,703
A schmear a day
keeps the hair away.

511
00:35:21,081 --> 00:35:23,042
Nice, Deavers, nice.

512
00:35:23,208 --> 00:35:24,918
Back me up,
I've never touched the stuff.

513
00:35:35,554 --> 00:35:37,431
<i>This is an urgent update</i>

514
00:35:37,514 --> 00:35:40,517
<i>for Colonel Pruitt, Thomas F...</i>

515
00:35:40,684 --> 00:35:43,812
<i>regarding the status
of the Lima Project.</i>

516
00:35:43,979 --> 00:35:46,106
<i>SPACECOM believes
it has detected</i>

517
00:35:46,190 --> 00:35:48,400
<i>a possible SOS signal...</i>

518
00:35:48,567 --> 00:35:51,445
<i>from the crew
of the Lima Project.</i>

519
00:35:51,612 --> 00:35:53,572
<i>The message could indicate</i>

520
00:35:53,656 --> 00:35:55,991
<i>that Commander H.
Clifford McBride...</i>

521
00:35:56,158 --> 00:36:00,579
<i>intentionally disabled
all external communications.</i>

522
00:36:00,663 --> 00:36:02,831
<i>Under such circumstances...</i>

523
00:36:02,998 --> 00:36:05,793
<i>the Commander may
have lost all control.</i>

524
00:36:05,959 --> 00:36:07,503
<i>If this is the case...</i>

525
00:36:07,670 --> 00:36:09,713
<i>and communication cannot be made</i>

526
00:36:09,797 --> 00:36:11,548
<i>through his son on Mars...</i>

527
00:36:11,715 --> 00:36:14,426
<i>then all other efforts
must be undertaken</i>

528
00:36:14,510 --> 00:36:16,303
<i>to destroy the Commander...</i>

529
00:36:16,470 --> 00:36:18,222
<i>and halt the surges.</i>

530
00:36:18,430 --> 00:36:20,808
<i>This message is top secret.</i>

531
00:36:23,936 --> 00:36:25,979
<i>What happened to my dad?</i>

532
00:36:27,439 --> 00:36:30,067
<i>What did he find out there?</i>

533
00:36:31,985 --> 00:36:33,987
<i>Did it break him?</i>

534
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:37,950
<i>Or was he always broken?</i>

535
00:36:48,627 --> 00:36:50,003
<i>My father...</i>

536
00:36:51,755 --> 00:36:55,134
<i>the most decorated astronaut
in the history of the program.</i>

537
00:36:57,511 --> 00:36:59,346
<i>U.S. Air Force Academy...</i>

538
00:36:59,513 --> 00:37:01,682
<i>his doctorate at MIT.</i>

539
00:37:03,142 --> 00:37:04,518
<i>He promised me that one day</i>

540
00:37:04,601 --> 00:37:06,103
<i>I could join him
in his pursuits...</i>

541
00:37:08,731 --> 00:37:10,607
<i>that he'd come back for me.</i>

542
00:37:12,943 --> 00:37:15,195
<i>And I believed him.</i>

543
00:37:17,406 --> 00:37:18,949
<i>First man to Jupiter.</i>

544
00:37:19,116 --> 00:37:20,868
<i>First to Saturn.</i>

545
00:37:21,034 --> 00:37:24,580
<i>And then... nothing.</i>

546
00:37:35,215 --> 00:37:37,217
Commence slow down,
booster three.

547
00:37:38,469 --> 00:37:39,636
We're slowing down.

548
00:37:39,803 --> 00:37:40,804
Yes, sir.

549
00:37:40,971 --> 00:37:43,849
Got a mayday
from another craft, sir.

550
00:37:44,016 --> 00:37:45,058
Captain, this is a classified mission,

551
00:37:45,142 --> 00:37:46,143
we cannot stop.

552
00:37:46,226 --> 00:37:48,520
Our destination is Mars.
Ersa Station.

553
00:37:49,229 --> 00:37:50,397
Major, this is a mayday.

554
00:37:50,481 --> 00:37:51,482
Stopping is protocol.

555
00:37:51,982 --> 00:37:53,734
Any supply craft
can answer that call.

556
00:37:53,901 --> 00:37:55,861
The mission
is the priority, Captain.

557
00:37:55,944 --> 00:37:57,571
Do you not hear what I'm saying?

558
00:37:57,738 --> 00:38:01,950
Major, with respect, as I say,
we are obligated to stop.

559
00:38:02,284 --> 00:38:03,869
As you're merely a passenger,

560
00:38:03,952 --> 00:38:06,413
I'm not sure
I comprehend your position.

561
00:38:06,580 --> 00:38:08,499
'Course, you are
well within your rights

562
00:38:08,582 --> 00:38:09,917
to take command of this craft...

563
00:38:10,083 --> 00:38:13,086
but if so, you will have to
reveal your objectives.

564
00:38:17,341 --> 00:38:19,259
Attend to the mayday.

565
00:38:19,426 --> 00:38:21,720
Command, craft
is registered as Norwegian.

566
00:38:21,887 --> 00:38:24,556
The <i>Vesta IX,</i>
orbiting asteroid Toro...

567
00:38:24,723 --> 00:38:26,266
registered for
biomedical research...

568
00:38:26,433 --> 00:38:28,977
on Comet 17-P, Holmes.
<i>Copy.</i>

569
00:38:29,812 --> 00:38:31,605
<i>Vesta IX,</i> we're responding

570
00:38:31,688 --> 00:38:33,106
to your distress call.

571
00:38:33,690 --> 00:38:35,567
Do you read?

572
00:38:37,402 --> 00:38:39,655
The distress call
is fairly recent.

573
00:38:40,781 --> 00:38:42,825
Maybe they were hit
by The Surge.

574
00:38:45,285 --> 00:38:48,080
Command, possible forced entry
to the <i>Vesta</i> required.

575
00:38:48,247 --> 00:38:49,832
Either First Lieutenant Stanford

576
00:38:49,915 --> 00:38:51,083
or I will take
a little spacewalk...

577
00:38:51,166 --> 00:38:52,543
and make our way
to the craft, over.

578
00:38:52,626 --> 00:38:53,627
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

579
00:38:55,546 --> 00:38:57,381
Donald, what are you thinking?

580
00:38:57,548 --> 00:38:58,966
Wanna go out there?

581
00:39:00,300 --> 00:39:02,803
Uh, yeah.
Doesn't matter to me.

582
00:39:04,513 --> 00:39:05,848
<i>He's scared.</i>

583
00:39:05,931 --> 00:39:06,932
Yeah, I know,

584
00:39:07,015 --> 00:39:08,725
my suit smells
like a locker room, too.

585
00:39:09,226 --> 00:39:11,186
Oh, hell, I could use
a good stretch anyway.

586
00:39:11,270 --> 00:39:14,064
<i>Most of us spend
our entire lives in hiding.</i>

587
00:39:14,690 --> 00:39:16,024
I'll accompany you, Captain.

588
00:39:16,191 --> 00:39:17,609
Very good.

589
00:39:46,221 --> 00:39:48,724
Vesta <i>lists 26 souls onboard.</i>

590
00:39:49,224 --> 00:39:51,184
<i>Craft registered for biomedical</i>

591
00:39:51,268 --> 00:39:52,728
<i>and animal research.</i>

592
00:40:07,576 --> 00:40:08,619
<i>Sorry about that little tiff</i>

593
00:40:08,702 --> 00:40:09,703
<i>back there, Major.</i>

594
00:40:10,412 --> 00:40:12,414
<i>I'm honored
to be out here with ya.</i>

595
00:40:13,832 --> 00:40:16,418
<i>You know, your dad
is the reason why</i>

596
00:40:16,501 --> 00:40:17,878
<i>a lot of us are doing
what we're doing.</i>

597
00:40:19,296 --> 00:40:21,340
<i>He went farther than anybody.</i>

598
00:40:22,174 --> 00:40:24,009
<i>He was the best of us.</i>

599
00:40:24,718 --> 00:40:26,386
<i>Imagine the things he saw.</i>

600
00:40:28,722 --> 00:40:30,098
<i>Imagine.</i>

601
00:40:34,227 --> 00:40:35,520
Vesta, <i>this is</i> Cepheus

602
00:40:35,604 --> 00:40:36,897
<i>responding to your
mayday signal.</i>

603
00:40:37,064 --> 00:40:38,482
<i>Do you read?</i>

604
00:40:41,234 --> 00:40:43,278
Cepheus, <i>the craft
is not responding.</i>

605
00:40:43,445 --> 00:40:45,072
<i>Forced entry required.</i>

606
00:40:45,989 --> 00:40:48,200
<i>I am now initiating
mayday entry code.</i>

607
00:41:37,874 --> 00:41:40,377
Vesta, <i>this is</i> Cepheus
<i>responding to your mayday.</i>

608
00:41:40,460 --> 00:41:41,503
<i>Do you read?</i>

609
00:41:53,682 --> 00:41:54,891
<i>Major, I'll take Truss 5.</i>

610
00:41:54,975 --> 00:41:56,977
<i>Why don't you start
with Truss 2?</i>

611
00:41:57,769 --> 00:41:59,771
<i>Don't wander off too far, now.</i>

612
00:42:03,275 --> 00:42:05,277
<i>Where is everybody?</i>

613
00:42:07,654 --> 00:42:10,115
Vesta, <i>this is</i> Cepheus
<i>responding to your mayday.</i>

614
00:42:10,198 --> 00:42:11,408
<i>Do you read?</i>

615
00:42:37,642 --> 00:42:39,644
<i>Tanner, McBride, check.</i>

616
00:42:42,647 --> 00:42:44,733
<i>Tanner, do you copy?</i>

617
00:42:48,445 --> 00:42:50,614
<i>Tanner, do you copy?</i>

618
00:43:14,262 --> 00:43:15,388
<i>Tanner?</i>

619
00:43:19,476 --> 00:43:20,477
<i>Tanner?</i>

620
00:43:41,331 --> 00:43:43,250
<i>Repeat, calling for Major McBride.</i>

621
00:43:43,333 --> 00:43:45,043
<i>Calling for Captain Tanner.</i>

622
00:44:12,612 --> 00:44:14,698
<i>Stay calm. I got you.</i>

623
00:44:14,865 --> 00:44:16,283
<i>Make it back.</i>

624
00:44:19,244 --> 00:44:21,788
Cepheus, <i>Captain was attacked
by a research primate.</i>

625
00:44:22,706 --> 00:44:24,499
<i>Emergency medical stand by.</i>

626
00:44:24,666 --> 00:44:26,084
<i>Attempting extraction now.</i>

627
00:44:59,701 --> 00:45:01,578
Cepheus, <i>this is SPACECOM.</i>

628
00:45:01,661 --> 00:45:03,246
<i>Real sorry about that setback.</i>

629
00:45:03,413 --> 00:45:05,957
<i>First Lieutenant Stanford is
in command of the craft...</i>

630
00:45:06,124 --> 00:45:09,169
<i>until Captain Tanner
can resume his duties. Over.</i>

631
00:45:10,545 --> 00:45:13,882
<i>SPACECOM, this is
First Lieutenant Stanford.</i>

632
00:45:14,716 --> 00:45:16,927
<i>Captain Tanner is dead.</i>

633
00:45:18,511 --> 00:45:20,430
<i>We take comfort knowing that</i>

634
00:45:20,513 --> 00:45:23,350
<i>the Captain embraced
the rewards...</i>

635
00:45:23,516 --> 00:45:25,560
<i>May the angels and
the saints come to meet you,</i>

636
00:45:25,644 --> 00:45:27,270
<i>as you go forth from this life.</i>

637
00:45:27,896 --> 00:45:30,023
<i>May you meet your Redeemer
face to face,</i>

638
00:45:30,106 --> 00:45:32,400
<i>and enjoy the vision
of God forever.</i>

639
00:45:33,193 --> 00:45:35,195
<i>Amen.</i>

640
00:45:57,842 --> 00:45:59,886
<i>McBride, Roy R.</i>

641
00:45:59,970 --> 00:46:02,722
<i>Are you ready for your
psychological evaluation?</i>

642
00:46:02,889 --> 00:46:04,266
Yes.

643
00:46:04,432 --> 00:46:06,518
<i>Please begin.</i>

644
00:46:06,685 --> 00:46:09,771
I am on my way to Mars.

645
00:46:10,438 --> 00:46:13,108
We answered
a mayday call, and...

646
00:46:13,275 --> 00:46:14,818
ended in tragedy.

647
00:46:14,985 --> 00:46:16,611
We lost the Captain.

648
00:46:17,654 --> 00:46:19,614
<i>Your answer is being processed.</i>

649
00:46:19,698 --> 00:46:20,699
<i>Please continue.</i>

650
00:46:23,159 --> 00:46:25,370
Well, that's it.
I mean, we...

651
00:46:25,537 --> 00:46:27,956
We go to work, we do our jobs...

652
00:46:29,457 --> 00:46:31,418
and then it's over.

653
00:46:31,584 --> 00:46:33,420
We're here, and then we're gone.

654
00:46:34,212 --> 00:46:35,255
<i>Please describe</i>

655
00:46:35,338 --> 00:46:37,465
<i>how the incident itself
affected you.</i>

656
00:46:39,217 --> 00:46:40,844
The attack...

657
00:46:42,887 --> 00:46:45,307
it was full of rage.

658
00:46:50,854 --> 00:46:53,064
I understand that rage.

659
00:46:56,693 --> 00:46:59,321
I've seen that rage
in my father...

660
00:47:00,405 --> 00:47:02,615
and I've seen that rage in me.

661
00:47:09,622 --> 00:47:12,000
Because I'm angry...

662
00:47:12,167 --> 00:47:13,793
that he took off.

663
00:47:16,546 --> 00:47:17,964
He left us.

664
00:47:21,509 --> 00:47:23,720
You know...

665
00:47:24,637 --> 00:47:25,889
but when I look at that anger,

666
00:47:25,972 --> 00:47:29,142
if I push it aside
and just put it away...

667
00:47:30,935 --> 00:47:33,938
all I see is hurt.

668
00:47:34,356 --> 00:47:38,568
I just see pain.

669
00:47:40,236 --> 00:47:41,571
I think it keeps me walled off...

670
00:47:41,654 --> 00:47:44,366
walled off from relationships...

671
00:47:44,532 --> 00:47:46,659
and opening myself up and,

672
00:47:46,743 --> 00:47:48,745
you know, really caring for someone.

673
00:47:51,915 --> 00:47:55,460
And I don't know
how to get past that.

674
00:47:55,627 --> 00:47:57,462
I don't know how
to get around that.

675
00:47:59,297 --> 00:48:01,508
And it worries me.

676
00:48:07,138 --> 00:48:09,015
And I don't wanna be that guy.

677
00:48:11,559 --> 00:48:13,395
I don't wanna be my dad.

678
00:48:15,105 --> 00:48:16,898
<i>Your psychological evaluation</i>

679
00:48:16,981 --> 00:48:18,066
<i>has been approved.</i>

680
00:48:18,233 --> 00:48:20,193
<i>If you wish to obtain
a complete...</i>

681
00:48:47,971 --> 00:48:49,139
<i>Major, would you commence</i>

682
00:48:49,222 --> 00:48:50,432
<i>auto-landing sequence?</i>

683
00:48:50,974 --> 00:48:52,475
<i>Copy.</i>

684
00:48:52,892 --> 00:48:54,352
<i>SPACECOM, we're approaching Mars.</i>

685
00:48:54,436 --> 00:48:56,604
<i>Ersa Station, south. Over.</i>

686
00:49:16,207 --> 00:49:17,792
<i>What the hell was that?</i>

687
00:49:19,085 --> 00:49:20,587
<i>Is that another surge?</i>

688
00:49:21,254 --> 00:49:23,923
<i>I think we just lost
primary electrical bus.</i>

689
00:49:25,049 --> 00:49:26,384
<i>Switching to bus Charlie.</i>

690
00:49:37,187 --> 00:49:38,521
<i>Captain, we're coming in
too hot.</i>

691
00:49:38,605 --> 00:49:40,440
<i>Our angle's off 20 degrees.</i>

692
00:49:44,277 --> 00:49:45,278
<i>I...</i>

693
00:49:46,488 --> 00:49:47,614
<i>Warning.</i>

694
00:49:47,697 --> 00:49:49,032
<i>Incorrect angle of descent.</i>

695
00:49:49,324 --> 00:49:50,450
<i>Go to manual.</i>

696
00:49:50,617 --> 00:49:52,660
<i>Warning.
Incorrect angle of descent.</i>

697
00:49:53,203 --> 00:49:54,412
<i>Warning.
Go to manual.</i>

698
00:49:54,496 --> 00:49:55,538
<i>Incorrect angle of descent.</i>

699
00:49:55,622 --> 00:49:56,706
<i>Captain, you need to do something.</i>

700
00:49:56,789 --> 00:49:57,916
<i>Incorrect angle of descent.</i>

701
00:49:57,999 --> 00:49:59,000
<i>I think I'm, uh...</i>

702
00:49:59,334 --> 00:50:00,418
<i>Go to manual.</i>

703
00:50:00,585 --> 00:50:02,086
<i>Danger.</i>

704
00:50:02,670 --> 00:50:04,547
<i>Danger.
Initiating manual override.</i>

705
00:50:04,714 --> 00:50:06,090
<i>Item 3-2...</i>

706
00:50:06,257 --> 00:50:08,510
<i>On my mark, execute.</i>

707
00:50:08,676 --> 00:50:11,179
<i>Mark. I have command
of the ship.</i>

708
00:50:11,679 --> 00:50:12,680
<i>Danger.</i>

709
00:50:15,141 --> 00:50:16,226
<i>Danger.</i>

710
00:50:16,309 --> 00:50:17,936
<i>2,000 meters.</i>

711
00:50:21,648 --> 00:50:23,483
<i>1,000 meters.</i>

712
00:50:24,651 --> 00:50:27,737
<i>Warning.
Incorrect angle of descent.</i>

713
00:50:31,908 --> 00:50:33,326
<i>Four...</i>

714
00:50:34,202 --> 00:50:35,620
<i>three...</i>

715
00:50:36,829 --> 00:50:38,248
<i>two...</i>

716
00:50:39,332 --> 00:50:40,333
<i>one.</i>

717
00:50:49,968 --> 00:50:51,386
<i>Contact.</i>

718
00:50:51,803 --> 00:50:53,221
<i>Engine shut down.</i>

719
00:50:56,057 --> 00:50:58,142
<i>Engine saved.
Your ship, Captain.</i>

720
00:51:00,603 --> 00:51:04,816
<i>Major, would you, uh, start
post-landing sequence, please?</i>

721
00:51:05,275 --> 00:51:06,693
<i>Copy that.</i>

722
00:51:26,296 --> 00:51:28,798
<i>Captain, I believe you
understand why I did that.</i>

723
00:51:29,841 --> 00:51:32,468
<i>I will not report it
to SPACECOM.</i>

724
00:51:41,978 --> 00:51:43,938
<i>This is an emergency alert.</i>

725
00:51:44,105 --> 00:51:46,816
<i>We have experienced
an external power surge.</i>

726
00:51:46,983 --> 00:51:48,818
<i>However, all underground systems</i>

727
00:51:48,901 --> 00:51:50,320
<i>remain fully operational.</i>

728
00:51:50,486 --> 00:51:52,697
<i>And there is no reason
for panic.</i>

729
00:51:52,864 --> 00:51:53,948
<i>My destination.</i>

730
00:51:54,032 --> 00:51:55,325
<i>We repeat,
all underground systems</i>

731
00:51:55,408 --> 00:51:56,534
<i>are fully operational.</i>

732
00:51:56,618 --> 00:52:00,163
<i>Seven weeks since Earth,
since air, since sun.</i>

733
00:52:00,246 --> 00:52:01,247
Hey, earthlings!

734
00:52:01,331 --> 00:52:02,373
Welcome to Ersa Research Station.

735
00:52:02,457 --> 00:52:04,542
<i>Trees and birds.</i>
I'm glad you made it.

736
00:52:04,626 --> 00:52:05,627
Thank you.

737
00:52:05,710 --> 00:52:07,170
I need your logs please.
Thank you.

738
00:52:07,253 --> 00:52:08,254
Sir?

739
00:52:08,338 --> 00:52:09,505
You got hit
by another surge, huh?

740
00:52:09,589 --> 00:52:10,715
Thank God we're underground,

741
00:52:10,798 --> 00:52:12,884
but the next one
could be the big one.

742
00:52:13,051 --> 00:52:15,470
I mean, it has been crazy
around here.

743
00:52:16,554 --> 00:52:18,640
<i>This was my dad's
last known stop.</i>

744
00:52:18,723 --> 00:52:19,807
Everyone's been running around

745
00:52:19,891 --> 00:52:21,643
like it's all gonna
end tomorrow.

746
00:52:22,518 --> 00:52:24,103
Sir, you can step over here.

747
00:52:24,270 --> 00:52:25,897
Put your palm down there.

748
00:52:27,523 --> 00:52:29,233
Very good. Thank you.

749
00:52:32,820 --> 00:52:35,031
All right, you guys are good
to move to the next concourse.

750
00:52:35,198 --> 00:52:36,491
The Director will meet you.

751
00:52:36,658 --> 00:52:37,784
Thank you.

752
00:52:52,590 --> 00:52:54,801
Welcome to the red planet, Major.

753
00:52:57,345 --> 00:53:01,140
I'm Helen Lantos,
Director of Operations here.

754
00:53:01,724 --> 00:53:04,936
Nice to see a new face
for a change.

755
00:53:05,478 --> 00:53:06,896
Follow me.

756
00:53:13,236 --> 00:53:15,363
You should be glad
you arrived safely.

757
00:53:15,530 --> 00:53:17,115
We had some kind of
cosmic storm.

758
00:53:17,281 --> 00:53:19,450
We lost three astronauts
trying to land.

759
00:53:20,243 --> 00:53:22,370
No one knows
what's causing them.

760
00:53:23,371 --> 00:53:24,497
Yes?
Major?

761
00:53:24,664 --> 00:53:26,290
We're glad you made it.

762
00:53:26,958 --> 00:53:28,501
Thanks, Helen,
we can take it from here.

763
00:53:28,960 --> 00:53:31,170
You're not authorized
at this level.

764
00:53:32,588 --> 00:53:33,756
Major?

765
00:53:35,675 --> 00:53:37,093
Well, thank you.

766
00:53:58,322 --> 00:54:00,908
<i>Stand by for secure
laser transmission.</i>

767
00:54:00,992 --> 00:54:02,994
<i>Attempting top secret link.</i>

768
00:54:03,161 --> 00:54:04,996
<i>Range: Neptune.</i>

769
00:54:30,021 --> 00:54:32,023
"This is Major Roy McBride.

770
00:54:32,690 --> 00:54:34,984
"I'm communicating through
a secure laser transmission...

771
00:54:35,151 --> 00:54:36,861
"sent from the communications hub

772
00:54:36,944 --> 00:54:39,864
"on Ersa Base,
North America sector, Mars.

773
00:54:40,031 --> 00:54:43,242
"I'm attempting to reach
Doctor Clifford McBride.

774
00:54:44,202 --> 00:54:46,829
"This is Doctor McBride's son, Roy.

775
00:54:52,794 --> 00:54:54,712
"Father, if you can hear me...

776
00:54:54,879 --> 00:54:57,089
"I'm attempting
to communicate with you.

777
00:54:57,840 --> 00:54:59,383
"SPACECOM wants you to know

778
00:54:59,467 --> 00:55:01,344
"that they are aware
of the disturbances...

779
00:55:01,511 --> 00:55:04,305
"and that it cannot be
your responsibility.

780
00:55:04,472 --> 00:55:05,890
"They would like
all information...

781
00:55:06,057 --> 00:55:08,017
"about attempts
that you are making

782
00:55:08,100 --> 00:55:09,894
"to ameliorate the situation.

783
00:55:11,896 --> 00:55:13,105
"They would also
like to tell you...

784
00:55:13,189 --> 00:55:15,107
"they're willing to help
and provide

785
00:55:15,191 --> 00:55:18,110
"for a rescue mission
if possible.

786
00:55:19,737 --> 00:55:22,281
"I hope you receive
this message.

787
00:55:22,365 --> 00:55:23,366
"Over and out."

788
00:55:27,078 --> 00:55:28,538
<i>Transmission sent.</i>

789
00:55:28,621 --> 00:55:29,914
<i>Awaiting response.</i>

790
00:55:41,843 --> 00:55:45,221
<i>Roy, we'll try again next cycle.</i>

791
00:55:54,105 --> 00:55:55,857
<i>They're using me.</i>

792
00:55:59,569 --> 00:56:01,320
<i>Goddamn them.</i>

793
00:56:05,533 --> 00:56:08,661
<i>I don't know
if I hope to find him...</i>

794
00:56:11,372 --> 00:56:13,791
<i>or finally be free of him.</i>

795
00:56:27,221 --> 00:56:28,556
<i>Dad...</i>

796
00:56:58,044 --> 00:56:59,921
Dad, I'd like to see you again.

797
00:57:10,556 --> 00:57:12,183
I recall how we used to watch

798
00:57:12,266 --> 00:57:13,476
black and white
movies together...

799
00:57:13,559 --> 00:57:15,728
and musicals were your favorite.

800
00:57:17,480 --> 00:57:19,607
I remember you tutoring
me in math.

801
00:57:22,568 --> 00:57:24,695
You instilled in me
a strong work ethic.

802
00:57:27,281 --> 00:57:30,785
"Work hard, play later,"
as you said.

803
00:57:35,915 --> 00:57:37,667
You should know
I've chosen a career

804
00:57:37,750 --> 00:57:40,086
that you would approve of.

805
00:57:40,252 --> 00:57:43,589
I've dedicated my life
to the exploration of space.

806
00:57:45,216 --> 00:57:46,550
And I thank you for that.

807
00:57:52,098 --> 00:57:53,849
So, I hope we can reconnect.

808
00:58:00,940 --> 00:58:02,483
Your loving son, Roy.

809
00:58:09,865 --> 00:58:11,325
<i>Transmission sent,</i>

810
00:58:11,409 --> 00:58:12,952
<i>awaiting response.</i>

811
00:59:07,173 --> 00:59:09,925
Thank you so much, Major,
for all your help.

812
00:59:10,092 --> 00:59:11,677
We'll be returning you
to the Earth

813
00:59:11,761 --> 00:59:13,220
in short order.
Thank you.

814
00:59:13,304 --> 00:59:16,474
Excuse me. Did you get a
response from my father?

815
00:59:16,640 --> 00:59:18,851
Major, your personal connection

816
00:59:18,934 --> 00:59:20,186
has made you unsuited...

817
00:59:20,269 --> 00:59:22,021
for continued service
on this mission.

818
00:59:29,361 --> 00:59:30,613
He answered me, didn't he?

819
00:59:30,696 --> 00:59:32,907
Major, we will let
you know any details

820
00:59:32,990 --> 00:59:34,283
as soon as possible.

821
00:59:34,450 --> 00:59:35,910
<i>Roy.</i>

822
00:59:36,410 --> 00:59:37,703
<i>Your pulse is very fast.</i>

823
00:59:37,787 --> 00:59:39,080
I know!

824
00:59:39,622 --> 00:59:41,707
There's also some issues
with your biorhythms.

825
00:59:41,874 --> 00:59:43,125
Those will need to be addressed

826
00:59:43,209 --> 00:59:45,002
before you can
safely return to Earth.

827
00:59:45,628 --> 00:59:46,712
<i>Would you please follow that man</i>

828
00:59:46,796 --> 00:59:48,923
<i>to take a psychological evaluation?</i>

829
00:59:53,803 --> 00:59:55,012
Major.

830
00:59:58,057 --> 00:59:59,058
Captain.

831
01:00:01,227 --> 01:00:02,603
Captain!

832
01:00:16,617 --> 01:00:19,161
<i>McBride, Roy R.
Are you ready</i>

833
01:00:19,245 --> 01:00:21,247
<i>for your psychological evaluation?</i>

834
01:00:23,290 --> 01:00:24,375
Yes.

835
01:00:24,458 --> 01:00:25,543
<i>How are you feeling</i>

836
01:00:25,626 --> 01:00:26,919
<i>in your current state?</i>

837
01:00:27,086 --> 01:00:28,546
Good, thank you.

838
01:00:28,629 --> 01:00:30,506
I will be returning
to Earth soon.

839
01:00:31,590 --> 01:00:35,219
I'm content to go home, and...

840
01:00:35,928 --> 01:00:36,929
<i>You have failed</i>

841
01:00:37,012 --> 01:00:38,430
<i>your psychological evaluation.</i>

842
01:00:38,597 --> 01:00:40,516
<i>You will be returned
to a comfort room</i>

843
01:00:40,599 --> 01:00:41,892
<i>until you are deemed...</i>

844
01:00:49,191 --> 01:00:50,484
Contact U.S. SPACECOM.

845
01:00:50,651 --> 01:00:52,903
<i>Provide contact and priority code.</i>

846
01:00:53,070 --> 01:00:54,280
Request emergency communication

847
01:00:54,363 --> 01:00:55,447
with General Stroud.

848
01:00:55,531 --> 01:00:59,243
Priority code,
Zulu-5-5-Bravo-Papa.

849
01:01:00,244 --> 01:01:02,538
<i>Your priority
code is no longer valid.</i>

850
01:01:02,705 --> 01:01:04,290
<i>Please contact a representative</i>

851
01:01:04,373 --> 01:01:06,000
<i>if this restriction is an error.</i>

852
01:01:30,107 --> 01:01:31,609
You're going back to Earth now?

853
01:01:34,987 --> 01:01:36,322
Can I help you?

854
01:01:39,575 --> 01:01:41,785
I've only been there once.

855
01:01:41,952 --> 01:01:43,787
As a child.

856
01:01:43,954 --> 01:01:45,497
I was born here.

857
01:01:48,375 --> 01:01:50,127
But I remember it so well.

858
01:01:51,754 --> 01:01:55,049
It was... beautiful.

859
01:01:58,427 --> 01:02:03,015
Ma'am, I'd really appreciate
my privacy right now.

860
01:02:03,974 --> 01:02:07,061
You're here because of
the cosmic rays, aren't you?

861
01:02:09,188 --> 01:02:10,564
That's classified.

862
01:02:12,608 --> 01:02:16,195
The craft you came in,
the <i>Cepheus...</i>

863
01:02:17,112 --> 01:02:20,908
they want me to requisition
it for deep space...

864
01:02:22,952 --> 01:02:24,620
with nuclear munitions onboard.

865
01:02:24,703 --> 01:02:25,829
Did you know that?

866
01:02:28,457 --> 01:02:30,584
It's for a search
and destroy mission.

867
01:02:33,837 --> 01:02:38,175
I am responsible for more
than 1,100 people here.

868
01:02:38,342 --> 01:02:39,927
On this base.

869
01:02:41,136 --> 01:02:44,014
Now, I need to know.

870
01:02:44,181 --> 01:02:46,100
Are we gonna die?

871
01:02:48,602 --> 01:02:50,521
I don't know what happens now.

872
01:02:54,483 --> 01:02:56,068
I know who you are.

873
01:02:58,279 --> 01:03:00,572
You are Clifford McBride's son.

874
01:03:01,991 --> 01:03:03,200
Yes.

875
01:03:06,161 --> 01:03:08,914
Well, then we're both victims
of the Lima Project.

876
01:03:11,000 --> 01:03:14,420
My parents left
for that expedition.

877
01:03:14,962 --> 01:03:18,299
You and I share
a great loss, Roy.

878
01:03:20,801 --> 01:03:22,428
Please, just tell me.

879
01:03:25,306 --> 01:03:28,600
The <i>Cepheus</i> leaves
in five hours.

880
01:03:36,608 --> 01:03:38,068
<i>You were right.</i>

881
01:03:38,152 --> 01:03:40,904
<i>The Surge is coming
from the Lima Project.</i>

882
01:03:42,156 --> 01:03:45,326
Ultimate catastrophe
is very possible.

883
01:03:47,578 --> 01:03:51,081
SPACECOM has determined
that I am unfit to carry on.

884
01:03:52,124 --> 01:03:53,625
That's all I know.

885
01:03:58,589 --> 01:04:00,841
I believe your father is alive.

886
01:04:02,384 --> 01:04:04,428
They never told you what
happened to him out there,

887
01:04:04,511 --> 01:04:05,846
did they?

888
01:04:31,955 --> 01:04:33,123
<i>U.S. Space Command</i>

889
01:04:33,207 --> 01:04:36,502
<i>Top Secret Briefing.
Alpha-Papa-4-2-7-8.</i>

890
01:04:36,585 --> 01:04:39,088
<i>Communications has received
the following mayday call...</i>

891
01:04:39,254 --> 01:04:40,631
<i>from the crew
of the Lima Project,</i>

892
01:04:40,714 --> 01:04:43,217
<i>under the command
of H. Clifford McBride.</i>

893
01:04:59,316 --> 01:05:00,734
<i>This is Clifford McBride,</i>

894
01:05:00,818 --> 01:05:03,362
<i>reporting from the Lima Project.</i>

895
01:05:04,905 --> 01:05:07,241
<i>I'm disclosing a tragedy.</i>

896
01:05:09,034 --> 01:05:11,120
<i>Here, on the edge
of our solar system,</i>

897
01:05:11,203 --> 01:05:12,329
<i>some of our people...</i>

898
01:05:12,496 --> 01:05:15,374
<i>have been unable to handle
the psychological distress...</i>

899
01:05:15,541 --> 01:05:19,503
<i>of being so far away from home.</i>

900
01:05:19,837 --> 01:05:22,297
<i>They desired to return to Earth,</i>

901
01:05:22,381 --> 01:05:24,383
<i>and I could not permit that.</i>

902
01:05:24,550 --> 01:05:26,802
<i>And I have to report the reality</i>

903
01:05:26,885 --> 01:05:27,928
<i>that they mutinied...</i>

904
01:05:28,095 --> 01:05:32,516
<i>committed acts of sabotage
trying to commandeer my ship.</i>

905
01:05:33,016 --> 01:05:36,228
<i>I was forced to react
with equal severity.</i>

906
01:05:36,854 --> 01:05:39,440
<i>I disabled one section</i>

907
01:05:39,523 --> 01:05:41,650
<i>of our station's
life support system...</i>

908
01:05:41,817 --> 01:05:42,818
<i>and without doubt,</i>

909
01:05:42,901 --> 01:05:45,571
<i>I did punish the innocent
along with the guilty.</i>

910
01:05:48,031 --> 01:05:50,742
<i>We will not turn back.</i>

911
01:05:50,826 --> 01:05:53,745
<i>We will venture further into space.</i>

912
01:05:53,912 --> 01:05:57,958
<i>We will find alien intelligence.</i>

913
01:05:58,750 --> 01:06:02,296
<i>I am forever driven
on this quest.</i>

914
01:06:11,346 --> 01:06:14,266
SPACECOM would never allow

915
01:06:14,349 --> 01:06:16,435
their image to be shattered...

916
01:06:18,145 --> 01:06:21,815
so they made him a hero
to protect themselves.

917
01:06:26,487 --> 01:06:31,617
Your father murdered my parents.

918
01:06:33,952 --> 01:06:36,705
That monster threatens us all.

919
01:06:40,125 --> 01:06:42,252
And now it's your burden.

920
01:06:56,517 --> 01:06:58,227
Can you get me on that ship?

921
01:07:02,189 --> 01:07:04,024
I can get you to the rocket.

922
01:07:05,901 --> 01:07:08,946
After that, you're on your own.

923
01:07:10,489 --> 01:07:12,074
I Will deal with him.

924
01:07:13,867 --> 01:07:16,411
I will deal with my father.

925
01:07:41,687 --> 01:07:43,438
This is a map
of an underground lake

926
01:07:43,522 --> 01:07:44,565
beneath the launchpad.

927
01:07:45,774 --> 01:07:48,151
You'll be able to access
the ship from there.

928
01:07:52,072 --> 01:07:53,574
We're approaching.

929
01:07:54,783 --> 01:07:56,785
They're gonna come for you,
you know.

930
01:07:57,953 --> 01:07:59,079
I know.

931
01:08:01,248 --> 01:08:02,708
I don't care anymore.

932
01:08:03,875 --> 01:08:06,878
I need to get back now,
do what I can.

933
01:08:08,130 --> 01:08:09,506
Good luck.

934
01:08:50,839 --> 01:08:52,966
<i>I'm being pulled,</i>

935
01:08:53,050 --> 01:08:55,677
<i>farther and farther
from the sun...</i>

936
01:09:00,891 --> 01:09:02,517
<i>to you.</i>

937
01:09:26,458 --> 01:09:28,168
<i>You're alive.</i>

938
01:09:31,296 --> 01:09:32,964
<i>All this time.</i>

939
01:09:42,265 --> 01:09:46,687
<i>I must accept the fact
I never really knew you.</i>

940
01:09:50,190 --> 01:09:52,067
<i>Or am I you...</i>

941
01:09:57,364 --> 01:10:00,325
<i>being pulled down
the same dark hole?</i>

942
01:10:03,995 --> 01:10:05,872
This is <i>Cepheus</i> Launch Control...

943
01:10:05,956 --> 01:10:09,334
<i>at T-minus 11 minutes,
7 seconds and counting.</i>

944
01:10:11,461 --> 01:10:13,547
<i>Our countdown continuing
and still aiming</i>

945
01:10:13,630 --> 01:10:15,048
<i>toward a planned
lift-off time...</i>

946
01:10:15,132 --> 01:10:17,801
<i>at 7:51, UTC.</i>

947
01:10:20,721 --> 01:10:23,181
<i>This is Launch Control.
Launch is imminent.</i>

948
01:11:17,235 --> 01:11:18,570
<i>Final checks from
the flight azimuth</i>

949
01:11:18,653 --> 01:11:20,155
<i>going on at this time...</i>

950
01:11:20,238 --> 01:11:22,657
<i>and we're also synchronizing
the clocks</i>

951
01:11:22,741 --> 01:11:23,909
<i>to the spacecraft...</i>

952
01:11:23,992 --> 01:11:27,370
<i>with the Mission Control
Center in Ersa.</i>

953
01:11:49,601 --> 01:11:51,019
<i>The engines are armed.</i>

954
01:11:51,561 --> 01:11:53,939
<i>Ten, nine...</i>

955
01:11:54,606 --> 01:11:58,109
<i>eight, seven, six...</i>

956
01:11:58,819 --> 01:12:01,279
<i>five, four...</i>

957
01:12:01,446 --> 01:12:02,989
<i>We have commit.</i>

958
01:12:03,156 --> 01:12:05,325
<i>...two, one.</i>

959
01:12:07,118 --> 01:12:08,870
<i>Lift-off.
We have lift-off.</i>

960
01:12:09,037 --> 01:12:11,540
<i>7:51, UTC.</i>

961
01:12:22,634 --> 01:12:24,052
<i>There's a breach.</i>

962
01:12:24,219 --> 01:12:25,470
<i>It's the airlock breach.</i>

963
01:12:27,180 --> 01:12:28,765
SPACECOM, this is <i>Cepheus.</i>

964
01:12:28,849 --> 01:12:30,225
<i>There's been a breach
in our airlock.</i>

965
01:12:30,392 --> 01:12:31,893
<i>How to proceed? Over.</i>

966
01:12:32,936 --> 01:12:34,437
<i>We see that, too.
We're checking it out.</i>

967
01:12:34,521 --> 01:12:35,522
<i>Stand by.</i>

968
01:12:38,108 --> 01:12:41,027
<i>SPACECOM, we need orders,
please. Over.</i>

969
01:12:41,194 --> 01:12:43,154
<i>McBride for Captain Stanford...</i>

970
01:12:43,822 --> 01:12:45,448
<i>Do you read?</i>

971
01:12:45,615 --> 01:12:47,409
<i>Jesus, it's McBride.</i>

972
01:12:47,576 --> 01:12:49,744
<i>He's breached
the goddamn airlock.</i>

973
01:12:50,245 --> 01:12:52,038
<i>Captain Stanford,
this is Major McBride.</i>

974
01:12:52,122 --> 01:12:53,290
<i>I am onboard.</i>

975
01:12:53,748 --> 01:12:56,376
<i>I am not a threat.
I repeat, I am not a threat.</i>

976
01:12:56,543 --> 01:12:58,712
<i>Major, your presence
is jeopardizing the mission.</i>

977
01:12:58,795 --> 01:12:59,838
<i>Stay where you are!</i>

978
01:13:00,005 --> 01:13:01,798
<i>Do not proceed any further.</i>

979
01:13:01,882 --> 01:13:03,550
<i>SPACECOM...
Stand by.</i>

980
01:13:03,633 --> 01:13:04,718
<i>SPACECOM, what are your orders?</i>

981
01:13:04,801 --> 01:13:06,052
<i>We're determining
the course of action here.</i>

982
01:13:06,136 --> 01:13:07,137
<i>We're about to switch over</i>

983
01:13:07,220 --> 01:13:08,221
<i>to long-range propulsion.</i>

984
01:13:08,305 --> 01:13:09,306
<i>Can you neutralize the threat?</i>

985
01:13:09,389 --> 01:13:11,349
<i>You'll never make it
to Neptune without me.</i>

986
01:13:11,433 --> 01:13:12,475
<i>You need me.</i>

987
01:13:12,809 --> 01:13:14,060
<i>Neutralize the Major.</i>

988
01:13:14,144 --> 01:13:16,897
<i>By any means necessary,
you must neutralize the Major.</i>

989
01:13:17,063 --> 01:13:18,273
<i>Copy that.</i>

990
01:13:18,899 --> 01:13:20,525
<i>Don't listen to them, Captain.</i>

991
01:13:20,692 --> 01:13:22,569
<i>I will take all accountability.</i>

992
01:13:22,736 --> 01:13:24,029
<i>Major, stay where you are.</i>

993
01:13:24,195 --> 01:13:26,656
<i>Do not proceed any further.
Do you read? Over.</i>

994
01:13:26,740 --> 01:13:28,033
<i>I say again,
neutralize the Major...</i>

995
01:13:28,116 --> 01:13:30,827
<i>by any means necessary.
Yoshida, I am not a threat.</i>

996
01:13:30,994 --> 01:13:33,079
<i>I am not the enemy.</i>

997
01:13:33,246 --> 01:13:34,623
<i>I am on your side.</i>

998
01:13:34,789 --> 01:13:36,166
<i>Major, we have our orders.</i>

999
01:13:36,333 --> 01:13:38,084
<i>Goddamn it! We're staging!</i>

1000
01:13:38,251 --> 01:13:40,128
<i>Frank, get out of there!
Deavers!</i>

1001
01:13:40,295 --> 01:13:41,379
<i>Get back in your seat!
Deavers, please!</i>

1002
01:13:52,766 --> 01:13:54,309
<i>Son of a bitch!</i>

1003
01:14:34,265 --> 01:14:35,684
<i>Air contaminated.</i>

1004
01:14:37,352 --> 01:14:38,645
<i>Get oxygen!</i>

1005
01:14:38,812 --> 01:14:40,480
<i>Yoshida, oxygen!</i>

1006
01:14:53,576 --> 01:14:56,287
<i>Ventilator. Ventilator.</i>

1007
01:14:58,248 --> 01:15:00,375
<i>Breathe.</i>

1008
01:15:01,543 --> 01:15:03,003
<i>Breathe in!</i>

1009
01:15:25,400 --> 01:15:27,110
<i>What have I done?</i>

1010
01:15:38,121 --> 01:15:40,290
<i>Mission, this is Major Roy McBride.</i>

1011
01:15:42,083 --> 01:15:44,919
<i>I boarded the</i> Cepheus
<i>against mission directives.</i>

1012
01:15:46,796 --> 01:15:49,007
I did not do so
with hostile intent.

1013
01:15:50,717 --> 01:15:54,387
<i>But because of my actions,
I regret to inform you...</i>

1014
01:15:55,096 --> 01:15:57,849
all crew members
are now deceased.

1015
01:16:00,935 --> 01:16:03,438
The flight recorder
will tell the story.

1016
01:16:05,440 --> 01:16:08,193
History will have to decide.

1017
01:16:11,154 --> 01:16:12,739
<i>I'm en route to Neptune.</i>

1018
01:16:12,822 --> 01:16:14,991
<i>I remain fully committed...</i>

1019
01:16:15,658 --> 01:16:18,369
<i>to the completion
of the mission...</i>

1020
01:16:20,622 --> 01:16:23,083
<i>namely to destroy</i>

1021
01:16:23,166 --> 01:16:25,502
<i>the Lima Project
in its entirety.</i>

1022
01:16:28,630 --> 01:16:30,256
I'm switching off all comms.

1023
01:16:30,423 --> 01:16:33,885
I'm going dark until final
approach to avoid detection.

1024
01:16:34,052 --> 01:16:35,428
Over and out.

1025
01:16:37,931 --> 01:16:39,557
<i>Estimated length of journey...</i>

1026
01:16:39,641 --> 01:16:44,646
<i>79 days, four hours,
eight minutes.</i>

1027
01:17:09,379 --> 01:17:11,047
<i>You seem really preoccupied</i>

1028
01:17:11,131 --> 01:17:12,549
<i>with your work.</i>

1029
01:17:14,717 --> 01:17:18,555
<i>I just feel like I'm
on my own all the time.</i>

1030
01:17:19,097 --> 01:17:20,932
<i>I don't know what we're doing.</i>

1031
01:17:21,891 --> 01:17:23,518
<i>You're so distant.</i>

1032
01:17:25,520 --> 01:17:28,731
<i>I mean, even when you're here,
I don't know where you are.</i>

1033
01:17:31,359 --> 01:17:33,945
<i>I feel like I'm looking
for you all the time...</i>

1034
01:17:35,238 --> 01:17:37,866
<i>trying to connect to you,
be close to you...</i>

1035
01:17:38,783 --> 01:17:40,785
<i>and it fucking sucks.</i>

1036
01:17:41,744 --> 01:17:43,371
<i>You know, I have my own life.</i>

1037
01:17:44,789 --> 01:17:47,375
<i>I'm my own person.</i>

1038
01:17:47,959 --> 01:17:50,170
<i>And I can't just wait for you.</i>

1039
01:17:58,511 --> 01:18:01,055
<i>Feeding tube activated.</i>

1040
01:18:15,612 --> 01:18:18,198
<i>...we have excited
real and enormous interest...</i>

1041
01:18:18,364 --> 01:18:20,825
<i>around the world,
and we're grateful for it.</i>

1042
01:18:20,992 --> 01:18:22,869
<i>See, we're doing big things
up here. Real big.</i>

1043
01:18:22,952 --> 01:18:25,872
<i>Namely, we are about to answer
the number one question...</i>

1044
01:18:25,955 --> 01:18:27,040
<i>when do we find</i>

1045
01:18:27,123 --> 01:18:29,334
<i>all the intelligent life out there?</i>

1046
01:18:29,500 --> 01:18:30,627
<i>And we know we will,</i>

1047
01:18:30,710 --> 01:18:32,253
<i>according to the Drake Equation.</i>

1048
01:19:01,282 --> 01:19:03,326
<i>What you see here</i>

1049
01:19:03,409 --> 01:19:06,329
<i>is the new starshade,
just ready to deploy.</i>

1050
01:19:06,621 --> 01:19:07,789
<i>You see it opening up</i>

1051
01:19:07,872 --> 01:19:11,834
<i>just like a prairie flower
in the springtime.</i>

1052
01:19:11,918 --> 01:19:14,045
<i>But I think you
are no longer deserving...</i>

1053
01:19:14,128 --> 01:19:15,463
<i>so I guess...</i>

1054
01:19:15,713 --> 01:19:16,798
<i>this is goodbye.</i>

1055
01:19:16,965 --> 01:19:18,091
<i>Roy?</i>

1056
01:19:28,518 --> 01:19:30,561
<i>...retired from
the program leaves me to doubt</i>

1057
01:19:30,645 --> 01:19:33,314
<i>not only your judgement,
but your character.</i>

1058
01:19:33,481 --> 01:19:34,816
<i>See, we're just out
from Mars now.</i>

1059
01:19:34,899 --> 01:19:35,942
<i>He's been to Mars?</i>

1060
01:19:36,025 --> 01:19:37,277
<i>Just on our way past Jupiter...</i>

1061
01:19:37,360 --> 01:19:38,653
<i>Do you wanna know a secret?</i>

1062
01:19:38,736 --> 01:19:40,196
<i>...eventually onto Neptune.</i>

1063
01:19:40,280 --> 01:19:41,823
<i>A, you're adorable</i>

1064
01:19:41,906 --> 01:19:42,991
<i>You have traded...</i>

1065
01:19:43,074 --> 01:19:44,242
<i>B, you're so beautiful</i>

1066
01:19:44,325 --> 01:19:45,535
<i>...a glimpse
of the infinite...</i>

1067
01:19:45,618 --> 01:19:48,413
<i>C, you're a cutie full of charms</i>

1068
01:19:48,579 --> 01:19:51,374
<i>D, you're delightful
and E, you're exciting and</i>

1069
01:19:51,457 --> 01:19:52,583
<i>I am free
of your moral boundaries.</i>

1070
01:19:52,667 --> 01:19:53,710
<i>I have total clarity.</i>

1071
01:19:53,793 --> 01:19:55,920
<i>F, you're a feather in my arms</i>

1072
01:19:56,087 --> 01:19:58,631
<i>I am on my way to Neptune...</i>

1073
01:19:58,798 --> 01:20:00,842
<i>Because we will find
our brothers and sisters...</i>

1074
01:20:01,009 --> 01:20:03,219
<i>The zero G
and the extended duration</i>

1075
01:20:03,303 --> 01:20:05,346
<i>of the journey
is affecting me...</i>

1076
01:20:05,513 --> 01:20:07,390
<i>both physically and mentally.</i>

1077
01:20:07,557 --> 01:20:08,933
<i>I am alone.</i>

1078
01:20:09,309 --> 01:20:10,768
<i>Something I always
believed I preferred.</i>

1079
01:20:10,935 --> 01:20:12,895
I am alone.

1080
01:20:13,062 --> 01:20:14,981
<i>But I confess...</i>

1081
01:20:16,190 --> 01:20:17,775
<i>it's wearing on me.</i>

1082
01:20:20,903 --> 01:20:23,781
<i>I am alone.
I am alone.</i>

1083
01:20:25,199 --> 01:20:26,826
Over and out.

1084
01:20:33,458 --> 01:20:35,626
<i>I've let so many people down.</i>

1085
01:20:35,793 --> 01:20:36,794
<i>Hi, Roy.</i>

1086
01:20:38,588 --> 01:20:39,839
<i>Um...</i>

1087
01:20:39,922 --> 01:20:41,132
<i>I know it's a little bit weird...</i>

1088
01:20:41,299 --> 01:20:42,550
<i>that I'm sending you this video,</i>

1089
01:20:42,633 --> 01:20:43,801
<i>and not talking to you
in person...</i>

1090
01:20:43,968 --> 01:20:46,679
I'm so selfish. I'm selfish.
I'm just so selfish.

1091
01:20:46,763 --> 01:20:49,640
I'm just a selfish person.

1092
01:20:56,939 --> 01:20:59,275
<i>And I know for
certain I am doing God's work.</i>

1093
01:20:59,359 --> 01:21:00,443
Forgiveness is bullshit.

1094
01:21:00,526 --> 01:21:02,111
<i>We will find
our brothers and sisters...</i>

1095
01:21:02,195 --> 01:21:03,321
<i>Exaltation!</i>

1096
01:21:38,898 --> 01:21:40,274
<i>Approaching location</i>

1097
01:21:40,358 --> 01:21:42,693
<i>determined by McBride, Roy R.</i>

1098
01:21:43,027 --> 01:21:46,280
<i>Retrieved, Mars secure
laser transmission.</i>

1099
01:21:50,576 --> 01:21:53,955
<i>Entering Neptune signal zone.</i>

1100
01:21:55,790 --> 01:21:59,794
Execute 72 plus 99.

1101
01:22:00,962 --> 01:22:02,380
<i>Executed.</i>

1102
01:22:09,345 --> 01:22:11,264
<i>Nuclear activation code</i>

1103
01:22:11,347 --> 01:22:15,435
<i>accessible through system file 52B.</i>

1104
01:22:39,709 --> 01:22:41,461
<i>Flight recorder,</i>

1105
01:22:41,544 --> 01:22:44,213
<i>the Lima Project's orbit
is degrading.</i>

1106
01:22:44,755 --> 01:22:46,674
<i>Its position has shifted somewhat</i>

1107
01:22:46,757 --> 01:22:48,759
<i>from the programmed coordinates.</i>

1108
01:22:50,178 --> 01:22:52,305
<i>I will need
to take a transport capsule</i>

1109
01:22:52,388 --> 01:22:54,599
<i>to maneuver
around Neptune's rings.</i>

1110
01:22:56,058 --> 01:22:58,519
<i>The</i> Cepheus <i>will remain
in autopilot</i>

1111
01:22:58,603 --> 01:23:00,688
<i>while I complete the mission.</i>

1112
01:23:21,459 --> 01:23:24,420
<i>All my life, I was terrified
to confront him.</i>

1113
01:23:26,797 --> 01:23:29,091
<i>I'm terrified even now.</i>

1114
01:23:37,433 --> 01:23:39,644
<i>What do I expect?</i>

1115
01:23:45,149 --> 01:23:50,404
<i>In the end, the son suffers
the sins of the father.</i>

1116
01:24:08,631 --> 01:24:12,468
<i>Warning. Power surge. CPU damaged.</i>

1117
01:24:12,552 --> 01:24:14,512
<i>Warning. Power surge.</i>

1118
01:24:45,251 --> 01:24:48,629
<i>Lima, Major McBride
of the</i> Cepheus.

1119
01:24:49,130 --> 01:24:52,133
<i>United States Armed Forces,
Space Division.</i>

1120
01:24:52,800 --> 01:24:57,221
<i>Attempting to contact
Dr. Clifford McBride. Over.</i>

1121
01:25:02,977 --> 01:25:05,730
<i>Lima,</i> Cepheus.
<i>Do you read? Over.</i>

1122
01:25:23,456 --> 01:25:26,459
<i>Craft damaged. Unable to dock.</i>

1123
01:29:16,355 --> 01:29:17,773
Roy?

1124
01:29:19,817 --> 01:29:21,819
Roy, is that you?

1125
01:29:24,989 --> 01:29:28,409
I have cataracts,
I don't see very well.

1126
01:29:40,129 --> 01:29:41,547
Hi, Dad.

1127
01:29:43,799 --> 01:29:45,217
You alone?

1128
01:29:46,135 --> 01:29:47,553
Oh, yeah.

1129
01:29:48,512 --> 01:29:51,348
Captain always goes down
with the ship.

1130
01:29:53,142 --> 01:29:55,978
I've been here
quite a while alone.

1131
01:29:57,271 --> 01:30:00,316
I'm trying to stop
this goddamn surge.

1132
01:30:03,110 --> 01:30:04,570
What happened?

1133
01:30:06,280 --> 01:30:10,910
My last loyal few
tried to escape.

1134
01:30:11,076 --> 01:30:13,287
And they started all this.

1135
01:30:15,873 --> 01:30:18,709
They caused a meltdown
out there, Roy.

1136
01:30:18,959 --> 01:30:23,088
We fought, and our struggle
caused catastrophe.

1137
01:30:23,797 --> 01:30:25,132
It's why I'm here.

1138
01:30:25,299 --> 01:30:27,134
I'm gonna stop it.

1139
01:30:27,885 --> 01:30:30,721
Get the two of us
back home, maybe.

1140
01:30:30,888 --> 01:30:32,264
Home?

1141
01:30:33,015 --> 01:30:34,516
Yep.

1142
01:30:36,769 --> 01:30:38,395
This is home.

1143
01:30:39,897 --> 01:30:43,108
This is a one-way voyage,
my son.

1144
01:30:44,109 --> 01:30:46,528
You're talking about Earth?

1145
01:30:48,280 --> 01:30:49,907
There was never anything
for me there.

1146
01:30:49,990 --> 01:30:52,117
I never cared about you,
or your mother...

1147
01:30:52,201 --> 01:30:55,663
or any of your small ideas.

1148
01:30:56,789 --> 01:30:58,415
For 30 years...

1149
01:30:58,582 --> 01:31:00,960
I've been breathing this air,
eating this food...

1150
01:31:01,043 --> 01:31:03,879
enduring these hardships...

1151
01:31:05,798 --> 01:31:08,425
and I never once thought
about home.

1152
01:31:12,221 --> 01:31:13,639
I know, Dad.

1153
01:31:28,445 --> 01:31:31,240
I knew this would
widow your mother...

1154
01:31:31,407 --> 01:31:33,534
and orphan you...

1155
01:31:36,537 --> 01:31:38,998
but I found my destiny.

1156
01:31:46,505 --> 01:31:48,382
So, I abandoned my son.

1157
01:31:53,220 --> 01:31:55,264
I still love you, Dad.

1158
01:32:04,815 --> 01:32:07,192
I'm taking you back.

1159
01:32:08,360 --> 01:32:10,863
Hmm... I have work to do.

1160
01:32:13,657 --> 01:32:16,702
I have infinite work to do.

1161
01:32:17,953 --> 01:32:20,456
I must find intelligent life.

1162
01:32:23,042 --> 01:32:24,877
It's time to go.

1163
01:32:26,962 --> 01:32:29,256
We don't have much time.

1164
01:32:39,099 --> 01:32:40,517
Come on.

1165
01:33:21,683 --> 01:33:24,728
I admire your courage
for coming alone, Roy...

1166
01:33:24,895 --> 01:33:26,814
traveling all this way...

1167
01:33:26,980 --> 01:33:29,108
following me here.

1168
01:33:31,735 --> 01:33:34,363
Makes me wonder what we could
have accomplished together.

1169
01:33:37,282 --> 01:33:38,450
But I guess...

1170
01:33:38,617 --> 01:33:41,578
the fates have deprived me

1171
01:33:41,662 --> 01:33:43,622
of the partner
I should have had.

1172
01:33:46,875 --> 01:33:49,294
If we'd had more
people like you...

1173
01:33:50,420 --> 01:33:52,005
we could have pressed on,

1174
01:33:52,089 --> 01:33:53,799
could've found
what we're looking for.

1175
01:33:57,177 --> 01:34:00,139
My crew examined all the data...

1176
01:34:00,305 --> 01:34:03,142
discovered no other
life out there.

1177
01:34:03,684 --> 01:34:05,519
No other consciousness.

1178
01:34:06,478 --> 01:34:08,188
They quit.

1179
01:34:14,653 --> 01:34:16,071
Sometimes...

1180
01:34:18,240 --> 01:34:21,535
the human will must overcome
the impossible.

1181
01:34:22,327 --> 01:34:25,873
You and I have to
continue on, Roy. Together.

1182
01:34:29,334 --> 01:34:32,921
To find what science claims
does not exist.

1183
01:34:35,048 --> 01:34:37,426
You and I, together, Roy.

1184
01:34:41,638 --> 01:34:44,850
Because the Lima Project
has told us...

1185
01:34:46,185 --> 01:34:49,605
that we're all alone
in the knowable universe.

1186
01:34:51,899 --> 01:34:53,525
I can't fail.

1187
01:34:56,111 --> 01:34:58,405
You can't let me fail, Roy.

1188
01:35:09,166 --> 01:35:10,751
Dad...

1189
01:35:10,918 --> 01:35:13,003
you haven't.

1190
01:35:13,837 --> 01:35:15,923
Now, we know...

1191
01:35:18,383 --> 01:35:20,928
we're all we've got.

1192
01:36:08,225 --> 01:36:11,520
<i>Armed.
T-minus three hours.</i>

1193
01:37:49,785 --> 01:37:51,536
<i>Dad! Stop!</i>

1194
01:38:09,763 --> 01:38:10,931
<i>Roy!</i>

1195
01:38:24,236 --> 01:38:25,362
<i>Let me go.</i>

1196
01:38:43,463 --> 01:38:45,882
<i>Let me go, Roy.</i>

1197
01:39:02,983 --> 01:39:05,110
<i>Roy, let me go.</i>

1198
01:39:05,569 --> 01:39:07,112
<i>Let me go, Roy.</i>

1199
01:39:08,196 --> 01:39:09,281
<i>Dad!</i>

1200
01:39:19,332 --> 01:39:21,209
<i>Let me go, Roy.</i>

1201
01:39:22,794 --> 01:39:24,212
<i>Unhook me.</i>

1202
01:39:24,963 --> 01:39:26,673
<i>Unhook me, son.</i>

1203
01:40:50,590 --> 01:40:52,175
<i>Why go on?</i>

1204
01:40:56,429 --> 01:40:58,348
<i>Why keep trying?</i>

1205
01:44:10,874 --> 01:44:12,834
<i>You're gathering my work, I see.</i>

1206
01:44:19,716 --> 01:44:22,051
<i>Data download initiated.</i>

1207
01:44:23,928 --> 01:44:26,848
We're a dying breed, Roy.

1208
01:44:40,528 --> 01:44:42,530
<i>He captured
strange and distant worlds</i>

1209
01:44:42,614 --> 01:44:45,116
<i>in greater detail
than ever before.</i>

1210
01:44:48,077 --> 01:44:51,831
<i>They were beautiful, magnificent...</i>

1211
01:44:51,998 --> 01:44:54,667
<i>full of awe and wonder.</i>

1212
01:44:56,336 --> 01:44:58,797
<i>But beneath
their sublime surfaces...</i>

1213
01:44:59,923 --> 01:45:01,633
<i>there was nothing.</i>

1214
01:45:02,133 --> 01:45:04,469
<i>No love or hate.</i>

1215
01:45:04,928 --> 01:45:07,388
<i>No light or dark.</i>

1216
01:45:08,556 --> 01:45:11,351
<i>He could only see
what was not there...</i>

1217
01:45:12,352 --> 01:45:14,854
<i>and missed what was
right in front of him.</i>

1218
01:46:42,859 --> 01:46:44,861
<i>Command, this is Major Roy McBride.</i>

1219
01:46:45,737 --> 01:46:47,906
<i>I made it to the Lima Project.</i>

1220
01:46:48,072 --> 01:46:49,365
<i>I am destroying the structure...</i>

1221
01:46:49,532 --> 01:46:53,244
to prevent any further surges
from reaching Earth...

1222
01:46:53,411 --> 01:46:56,247
using the nuclear munitions onboard.

1223
01:46:56,915 --> 01:46:58,917
I will attempt to return

1224
01:46:59,000 --> 01:47:01,586
using the explosion
as my primary propellant.

1225
01:47:02,962 --> 01:47:05,298
In the case I do not survive,

1226
01:47:05,381 --> 01:47:08,134
I've retrieved significant
data from the Lima.

1227
01:47:08,468 --> 01:47:11,262
And all efforts should be made
to retrieve my craft.

1228
01:47:14,015 --> 01:47:15,850
<i>Trajectory, Earth.</i>

1229
01:47:15,934 --> 01:47:19,395
<i>2.714 billion miles.</i>

1230
01:47:26,861 --> 01:47:30,448
I am looking forward to
the day my solitude ends.

1231
01:47:32,784 --> 01:47:34,410
And I'm home.

1232
01:47:37,747 --> 01:47:42,919
<i>Detonation in T-minus 20 seconds.</i>

1233
01:49:30,777 --> 01:49:31,778
<i>The aboard advisory system.</i>

1234
01:49:31,944 --> 01:49:33,029
<i>Affirmative, we're ready.</i>

1235
01:49:33,196 --> 01:49:34,697
<i>USP flight system is operational.</i>

1236
01:49:34,781 --> 01:49:35,782
<i>Thank you.</i>

1237
01:49:35,948 --> 01:49:37,575
<i>K-R-5 on the 4-2.</i>

1238
01:49:37,658 --> 01:49:38,743
<i>Good copy, flight.</i>

1239
01:49:38,826 --> 01:49:40,328
<i>We're ready to go.</i>

1240
01:50:27,166 --> 01:50:28,167
<i>Coming in, clean.</i>

1241
01:50:28,459 --> 01:50:30,294
<i>Copy that. Thanks.</i>

1242
01:50:31,420 --> 01:50:34,173
<i>One ready to go.
Data is good.</i>

1243
01:50:34,340 --> 01:50:36,300
<i>We have all good. All good.</i>

1244
01:51:14,338 --> 01:51:16,048
You're all right, Major.

1245
01:51:35,568 --> 01:51:39,363
<i>I'm steady, calm.</i>

1246
01:51:40,364 --> 01:51:43,117
I slept well. No bad dreams.

1247
01:51:45,620 --> 01:51:48,831
I am active and engaged.

1248
01:51:52,585 --> 01:51:54,003
<i>I'm aware of my surroundings</i>

1249
01:51:54,086 --> 01:51:56,505
<i>and those in my immediate sphere.</i>

1250
01:51:58,216 --> 01:51:59,717
I'm attentive.

1251
01:52:04,013 --> 01:52:05,723
<i>I'm focused on the essential...</i>

1252
01:52:05,890 --> 01:52:08,226
<i>to the exclusion of all else.</i>

1253
01:52:24,992 --> 01:52:27,912
I'm unsure of the future...

1254
01:52:28,079 --> 01:52:29,580
but I'm not concerned.

1255
01:52:35,127 --> 01:52:38,005
I will rely
on those closest to me.

1256
01:52:42,635 --> 01:52:44,845
<i>And I will share
their burdens...</i>

1257
01:52:53,312 --> 01:52:54,981
as they share mine.

1258
01:53:00,319 --> 01:53:01,654
I will live...

1259
01:53:03,197 --> 01:53:04,991
and love.

1260
01:53:11,914 --> 01:53:13,165
Submit.

